esting</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">attribclosingadj</span><span class="ttl">tools/pipeline/check_commit_attribution.py: its CLOSURE regex `\b(closed|closes|closing)\b` matches &#x27;closing&#x27; used as an ADJECTIVE (&#x27;closing verdict&#x27;, &#x27;closing pass&#x27;), so a commit subject that names a row and mentions its closing pass reads as a closure claim -- HARD, against every later commit</span><span class="tip">tools/pipeline/check_commit_attribution.py: its CLOSURE regex `\b(closed|closes|closing)\b` matches &#x27;closing&#x27; used as an ADJECTIVE (&#x27;closing verdict&#x27;, &#x27;closing pass&#x27;), so a commit subject that names a row and mentions its closing pass reads as a closure claim -- HARD, against every later commit — witness: harness: measured 2026-09-18 -- 8bd97e4&#x27;s subject &#x27;shipped with the width row its own closing verdict owed&#x27; made section L go HARD (&#x27;commit says CLOSED; row is in work&#x27;) for every commit after it; worked around with lcaisalane.reopened naming 8bd97e4</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED]  Filed by GXEMUL (2) [e8a2bc] from the 3c41f01 dry precommit.  The regex cannot tell a closure claim from the adjective; a word-list tweak (drop `closing`, or require it before a row id) would fix it, but it is a harness change owing two negative controls, so it is FILED for whoever owns the checker rather than patched in a records commit.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">fbnobuild</span><span class="ttl">gate_offline.sh&#x27;s fbpending_bound lanes on a host with no build/ objects: the #442 main lane `note`s (the gate stays PASS, rc 0) while #537&#x27;s self-mutant lane SETUPs under the row name &#x27;the detector still detects&#x27; -- the only red sits on a row named for something else -- and a retained diff_fbpending_bound.log can satisfy the SELFCHECK ran-its-sentinel row</span><span class="tip">gate_offline.sh&#x27;s fbpending_bound lanes on a host with no build/ objects: the #442 main lane `note`s (the gate stays PASS, rc 0) while #537&#x27;s self-mutant lane SETUPs under the row name &#x27;the detector still detects&#x27; -- the only red sits on a row named for something else -- and a retained diff_fbpending_bound.log can satisfy the SELFCHECK ran-its-sentinel row — witness: none</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed from the Opus seat&#x27;s #537 pass 2 (P4, MEASURED with lib.sh: a note()-only gate ends PASS rc 0, degrade() ends SKIP rc 77) and widened by fable5&#x27;s ruling on D1.  REACHABLE only when gate 1 failed, skipped or was not selected (run.sh runs every gate whatever the previous rc -- codex), or on a standalone bare-host run; the stale-log half needs a retained $LOGDIR.  Also carries F14&#x27;s freshness clause (standalone runs link whatever build/ holds; only the battery&#x27;s gate 1 rebuilds it from est/ and asserts 223 objects) and O7&#x27;s stray regress/dev_footbridge.c, which the #442 lane would compile SILENTLY (gcc searches the including file&#x27;s directory first) while the SM lane never reaches it -- the two lanes would test different code.  A gate-behaviour change owing two negative controls, so it is its own round, not a rider on #537. || 2026-09-19 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] L4 on this row&#x27;s own text: the stray regress/dev_footbridge.c reaches BOTH lanes (codex J2, #538 farm), not one.  Repair draft (codex L2, 2026-09-19): one object snapshot shared by both lanes, FB_BUILD_SRC override, degrade in both lanes, truncate the log before the main lane, SC_PREREQ_SKIPPED so the SELFCHECK manifest row says &#x27;not run (declared missing prerequisite)&#x27; rather than reading the previous run.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</s