te_offline_20260918_1959.log -- the only FAIL of 346</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed on fable5&#x27;s finding that the two exemptions have NO queue row (OUTSTANDING_BUGS names SC_EXEMPT only generically).  codex and grok found the red on the #536/#537 §F2 pass; gate 2 run 2026-09-18 19:59 is its first OBSERVATION: 1 FAIL of 346, got= ieee_store wdc_identify want=none.  The 2026-09-02 dates were set in 7e3b120 (2026-08-19) with the fortnight the owner chose for SM_EXEMPT.  The re-date ships as its own commit, by owner ruling. || 2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Owner ruling 2026-09-25 carried out, half 1: #550 re-dated ieee_store to 2026-12-10 with its reason standing (gate_offline.sh&#x27;s SC_EXEMPT).  wdc_identify is #551&#x27;s, to be FIXED rather than re-dated; until #551 lands its entry stays valid ON 2026-09-27. || 2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Owner ruling 2026-09-25 carried out, half 2: #551 FIXED wdc_identify (a self-check on its two comparators, a covered-failure report, moved to SC_COVERED) instead of re-dating it.  The row stays OPEN for ieee_store (due 2026-12-10).</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">alphaifetchkill</span><span class="ttl">cpu_dyntrans.c:729-733: a failed INSTRUCTION-FETCH translation that raises no exception ends the host (&quot;FATAL: could not find physical address of the exception handler?&quot;; exit(1)) -- and on Alpha, which delivers no memory-management fault, every cold instruction-fetch miss takes that path</span><span class="tip">cpu_dyntrans.c:729-733: a failed INSTRUCTION-FETCH translation that raises no exception ends the host (&quot;FATAL: could not find physical address of the exception handler?&quot;; exit(1)) -- and on Alpha, which delivers no memory-management fault, every cold instruction-fetch miss takes that path — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/witness_HEAD_20260918/vm_neighbour_measure.frozen.py -- rung 3, session B: paging armed (the arming control keeps its sentinel), one JMP to a raw VA -&gt; two `wasn&#x27;t found&#x27; lines for exactly that VA, the FATAL text, wait status 256 (RESULT.out, transcript_B.txt) — note: [2026-09-19] #542 queued after #541 (it also corrects #541&#x27;s #194 comment); drafts in _scratchpad/waifk/.  FOUND 2026-09-18 by GXEMUL (2) [e8a2bc] while filling the alphavmkill brief, WITNESSED at rung 3 the same evening on the committed binary (no build).  DYNTRANS_PC_TO_POINTERS_GENERIC assumes a failed fetch translation raised an exception and moved the PC; it retries at cpu-&gt;pc and, on a second failure, fatal()s and exit(1)s.  alpha_translate_v2p fails WITHOUT moving the PC, so the retry is the same miss.  RESEARCH: codex_research_jA_20260918.txt (a bare `running = 0&#x27; falls through with no paddr; a bare `return&#x27; leaves next_ic unset).  PASS 1 (panel_20260919_003152, ten answers + fable5 LAST): option (e), GENERIC, THREE hunks -- stop the CPU with next_ic = &amp;nothing_call (no +1), an entry guard in run_instr, and an epilogue guard keyed on the sentinel (NEVER on !running).  The round is next after #541.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED]  Filed by GXEMUL (2) [e8a2bc] from the records batch of the #538 commit.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — fable5 RULED LAST (identity verified: claude-fable-5-1).  (e), GENERIC, THREE hunks -- D3 REVERSED: the epilogue&#x27;s PC sync truncates a size_t difference into `int low_pc&#x27;, so under the sentinel the PC is garbage ~2^-21 per run and a PC row is a check that cannot fail; the owed guard is keyed on next_ic == &amp;nothing_call, NEVER on !running (a device can clear running mid-block while real instructions still execute).  The kill mutant is the licensed composite {guard removed + cur_ic_page = &amp;nothing_call}.  The same probabilistic clobber exists on three shipped stop paths (unimplemented instruction, call_pal HALT, ARM Thumb) -- recorded as fact. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/fable5_p1.md  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/fable5_p1.md]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1, Opus 5 (resumed; READ-ONLY).  VERDICT: (e), GENERIC -- the exact two-hunk shape: in pc_to_pointers, running = 0, next_ic = &amp;nothing_call (NOT +1), cur_ic_page and pc untouched, return; in run_instr, return 0 after the entry update when stopped.  A per-architecture table shows only Alpha reaches :729.  Witness defects: a page-aligned JMP target and no planted marker.  NEW: ARM/PPC exception-vector recursion (-&gt; excvecrecurse). — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/opus5_p1.md  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/opus5_p1.md]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1, the DEDICATED cxlaunch job.  VERDICT: (e), Alpha-only preferred -- but no candidate ships verbatim: the copied stop sequence omits the immediate `nothing&#x27; execution (:2034) and so leaves next_ic one-past nothing_call. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/codex_advaifkp1.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/codex_advaifkp1.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1.  VERDICT: (e) GO-WITH-CHANGES -- run_instr needs an immediate return when !running, else the unrolled loop spins on nothing_call and the epilogue&#x27;s low_pc recalculation clobbers cpu-&gt;pc. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/agy.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/agy.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1.  VERDICT: (e) -- the Alpha translator fails without moving the PC, so the retry is the same miss; stop like the unimplemented-instruction path, but do not copy its next_ic++. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/grok.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/grok.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1, kimi-k3:cloud SUBSTITUTE (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: (e), ungated/generic -- Alpha-gating rests on a derivation that omits whether the other architectures&#x27; handler VAs translate. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_kimi.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_kimi.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1 (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: (e), generic -- a three-site patch: the stop, a harmless filler for the loop&#x27;s unconditional next_ic dereference, and a guarded epilogue PC reconstruction. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_glm.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_glm.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1 (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: (e) -- the only packet-supported safe stop, provided the shape preserves the faulting PC. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_deepseek.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_deepseek.txt]</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — CONFIRMED — PASS 1 (PACKET-FED).  VERDICT: NOT-RATIFY -- (e) underspecified as briefed (cur_ic_page, the accounting reset, the PC reconstruction).  Answered by the consolidated shape the adjudication ruled on. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_minimax.txt  [durable copy: regress/artifacts/alphaifetchkill/p1_20260919/panel_20260919_003152/ollama_minimax.txt]</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ptywaitstatus</span><span class="ttl">regress/*.py pty probes: the emulator child&#x27;s WAIT STATUS does not reach the liveness verdict in 56 of 73 pty probes -- a host death AFTER the final observation passes, and a dead attempt whose last print is missing can still qualify for a retry</span><span class="tip">regress/*.py pty probes: the emulator child&#x27;s WAIT STATUS does not reach the liveness verdict in 56 of 73 pty probes -- a host death AFTER the final observation passes, and a dead attempt whose last print is missing can still qualify for a retry — witness: harness: the codex seat&#x27;s in-memory mock of lca_widewrite_probe.py&#x27;s real session() (#538 pass 2, panel_20260918_221636/codex.txt); the fix measured both ways (clean run -&gt; status 0, alphavmkill&#x27;s exit(1) -&gt; 256) — note: [2026-10-02] RE-GRADED med -&gt; HIGH by #554 from the Astra review campaign (harness, HARNESS_DISPOSITIONS.md:1029-1030 (GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s amendments to `hpcc2widthprobe:F2` and `hppcroundingprobe:F2`): the class lets an emulator death after the last observation pass a probe&#x27;s verdict.  THE HIGH IS DISPUTED: the raise is Astra&#x27;s own, and the grok seat&#x27;s first-hand ruling (regress/artifacts/astrafiling_20261002/grok/grok_filehigh3.txt) is HIGH ONLY ON THE RE-INTRODUCTION RULE -- no live process end on the paths it read -- which is the rule question of the ten disputed harness rows that #554 files.  agy&#x27;s facts at the two sites the re-grade names (regress/artifacts/astrafiling_20261002/agy/agy_highfacts2.txt), verbatim, both sites: &quot;Q1: CAN PASS | Q2: NO LONGER | Q3: NONE FOUND&quot; -- Q1 the check on a real emulator death, Q2 the protected path today, Q3 a live instance; the files are under regress/artifacts/astraretro_20260926/ and astraretro_harness_20260926/).  CENSUS at cdbe7d7 over every top-level regress/*.py calling pty.fork (73): USED 16, BOUND-UNUSED 2 (arm_msrmode_probe.py, untracked; sh_pclock_probe.py binds `st&#x27; at :170 and returns without it at :173), BARE 39, NEVER REAPED 16.  *** My first deriver said 17/1: it counted sh_pclock&#x27;s `st = 0&#x27; reassignment as a use -- a correlate standing in for the class. ***  The peer&#x27;s codex J6 READING (regress/artifacts/cxfarm/r_20260918_2243/out/codex_j6_ptydeath.txt; durable copy: regress/artifacts/ptywaitstatus/codex_j6_ptydeath_20260918.txt): ALL 55 non-USED files left after e8a2bc&#x27;s two fixes have the late-death blind spot, 0 covered by another channel, 0 N/A; worst four sh_intprio_probe.py, lca_confwidth_probe.py (:216), fbpending_witness.py, sh4_pcic_probe.py.  INDEPENDENTLY MEASURED by the Opus seat on n6 pass 1 (the peer&#x27;s; _scratchpad/n6/opus_p1_20260919/OPUS_SUMMARY.md, M4; durable copy with #539): fbpending_drain_probe.py:405 and fbpending_witness.py:353 discard the waitpid status, no WEXITSTATUS in either, while footbridge_sites_probe.py:208 checks text AND status.  FIXED in #538&#x27;s lca_widewrite_probe.py and in the unshipped #540/#541 probes; the two fbpending probes are fixed in #539 (the peer).  REMEDY: after `quit&#x27;, DRAIN THE PTY TO EOF, then close and reap and require WIFEXITED &amp;&amp; status 0 -- draining first matters (closing the master first SIGHUPs the child).  POLICY: each round touching a member checks it; no sweep (it would change 56 instruments).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — [NOT A PANEL STAGE: NO PANEL CONVENED]  Filed by GXEMUL (2) [e8a2bc] from the records batch of the #538 commit. || 2026-09-19 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Two members of this class FIXED by #539 (fbpending_drain_probe.py, fbpending_witness.py; and footbridge_sites_probe.py&#x27;s teardown bounded): drain to EOF, close, bounded reap, exit/signal on every session-return path, K rows require the complaint AND exit 1, surviving arms exit 0.  Measured: x_exit2 and y_sigkill each red 3/3 K rows (table 2).  fable5 p1 F11: the text must be AND-ed in, and the old 0.3 s sleep-then-close was a load-sensitive oracle.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td cl