sertion keeps every count, so a detector edit that swaps a scenario out is invisible to the gate.  Found by the dedicated codex reading on #545&#x27;s first repair (task 4).  Not a floor question for #545 (an edit to the detector, not to the product).  Fix shape: pin a digest of the sorted green-name list per family.  And the gate&#x27;s own footbridge &#x27;Not covered&#x27; summary lists less than the detector&#x27;s NOT COVERED contract (the Opus seat, #545 3d&#x27;s pass, T11) -- a records fix for the same commit that fixes this.</span><span class="tip">gate_offline.sh pins the #545 footbridge families by the COUNT of distinct green row names (fb_distinct at 864 rows: P 78, X1-X8 440, X6 248, X7 148, X8 6, X9 100, X10 72, X11 80, X12 20, X13 20, X14 21), not by WHICH names -- a required row replaced by another uniquely-named passing assertion keeps every count, so a detector edit that swaps a scenario out is invisible to the gate.  Found by the dedicated codex reading on #545&#x27;s first repair (task 4).  Not a floor question for #545 (an edit to the detector, not to the product).  Fix shape: pin a digest of the sorted green-name list per family.  And the gate&#x27;s own footbridge &#x27;Not covered&#x27; summary lists less than the detector&#x27;s NOT COVERED contract (the Opus seat, #545 3d&#x27;s pass, T11) -- a records fix for the same commit that fixes this.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></t