loor ends at the five decline arms; the IRQ/FIQ enable arms (+0x188/+0x288) share no case with a decline, so a `len == 4` conjunct on their direction tests, on the write-data fetch with the Clear address exempted, or `len != 8` on the fetch, passes all 864 rows (measured, regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/closing_20260923/CL.log), and IRQEnable&#x27;s 8-byte read (an LDRD at +0x188) is read by no row.  An LDRD/STRD at +0x188 or +0x288 -- or at +0x18c/+0x28c, which the ARM load/store unit aligns down onto them -- is a guest input.  Disclosed in the contract.  Fix shape: X9/X10 rows for the enable arms at width 8 and the narrow Set/FIQ writes, each with a measured variant.</span><span class="tip">dev_footbridge.c: #545&#x27;s floor ends at the five decline arms; the IRQ/FIQ enable arms (+0x188/+0x288) share no case with a decline, so a `len == 4` conjunct on their direction tests, on the write-data fetch with the Clear address exempted, or `len != 8` on the fetch, passes all 864 rows (measured, regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/closing_20260923/CL.log), and IRQEnable&#x27;s 8-byte read (an LDRD at +0x188) is read by no row.  An LDRD/STRD at +0x188 or +0x288 -- or at +0x18c/+0x28c, which the ARM load/store unit aligns down onto them -- is a guest input.  Disclosed in the contract.  Fix shape: X9/X10 rows for the enable arms at width 8 and the narrow Set/FIQ writes, each with a measured variant.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><