ridge.c: WHICH interrupt a narrow IRQ Clear write drives is unobserved -- `INTERRUPT_ASSERT(*(len &lt; 4 ? &amp;d-&gt;timer_irq[0] : &amp;d-&gt;irq))` in the Clear arm passes all 864 rows (XC_dest, r3c/r3d tables): X14 counts the CPU line apart from the timer interrupts only at len 4, and X9-X13 count every call on one shared pair.  Disclosed (the Clear write&#x27;s body is not an edited line).  Options: re-wire X9-X13&#x27;s d-&gt;irq to X14&#x27;s CPU counter pair (zero new rows; X12/X13&#x27;s narrow Clears then see the destination -- the Opus seat, 3c&#x27;s pass) or one len-1 Clear row on X14&#x27;s split counters (codex, grok, agy, minimax); either owes a table.</span><span class="tip">dev_footbridge.c: WHICH interrupt a narrow IRQ Clear write drives is unobserved -- `INTERRUPT_ASSERT(*(len &lt; 4 ? &amp;d-&gt;timer_irq[0] : &amp;d-&gt;irq))` in the Clear arm passes all 864 rows (XC_dest, r3c/r3d tables): X14 counts the CPU line apart from the timer interrupts only at len 4, and X9-X13 count every call on one shared pair.  Disclosed (the Clear write&#x27;s body is not an edited line).  Options: re-wire X9-X13&#x27;s d-&gt;irq to X14&#x27;s CPU counter pair (zero new rows; X12/X13&#x27;s narrow Clears then see the destination -- the Opus seat, 3c&#x27;s pass) or one len-1 Clear row on X14&#x27;s split counters (codex, grok, agy, minimax); either owes a table.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><t