="0"><span class="rid">fblatchhistory</span><span class="ttl">dev_footbridge.c: a warn-once latch that re-arms after more repeats than any row makes passes all 864 rows -- `else if (!(d-&gt;warned_irq_status_w++ &amp; 3))` announces at the first decline and again at the fifth, and no instance declines one site five times (X6 first and repeat; X11 pairs; P1 four) (R3D_LH1, r3d_20260923; codex&#x27;s dedicated job, 3c&#x27;s pass).  Clause (e): the latch test partitions {0, nonzero} and both are rowed; a longer history is unbounded (`&amp; 7` needs nine).</span><span class="tip">dev_footbridge.c: a warn-once latch that re-arms after more repeats than any row makes passes all 864 rows -- `else if (!(d-&gt;warned_irq_status_w++ &amp; 3))` announces at the first decline and again at the fifth, and no instance declines one site five times (X6 first and repeat; X11 pairs; P1 four) (R3D_LH1, r3d_20260923; codex&#x27;s dedicated job, 3c&#x27;s pass).  Clause (e): the latch test partitions {0, nonzero} and both are rowed; a longer history is unbounded (`&amp; 7` needs nine).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Researc