s POSITIVE classifications on Python tokens (regress/census_tokens.py: a comment, a string or a docstring is not code; statement boundaries kept; per-occurrence counts), which closed the comment / string / docstring and most spacing evasions pass 2 and F2 measured.  STILL OPEN, each measured passing all 12 readiness rows on the shipped F6e (regress/artifacts/hygienecensus_20260923/controls_c6e/TABLE.txt, the F2 suite): e9, RANKED FIRST -- the TEXTUAL counts are LINE-based and key on `endswith(`, so a space before the paren (`buf.endswith (&quot;&gt;&quot;)`, the #37 bare defect behind one space) or a backslash continuation (t_bsl) removes a call from all of them; another receiver name (e_e1, n3h); `strip()` or `rstrip(&quot;\r\n&quot;)` for `rstrip()` (e_e5, n3f); a slice compare (e_e4; n10, `buf.rstrip()[-1:] == &quot;&gt;&quot;`, the bare defect again); a parenthesised receiver (n3b, n3c); a regex readiness test (n3i); readiness moved into a helper module (n3k, n3k2 -- no count sees WHICH probe a helper serves); a probe forking with `forkpty` (n4a -- outside the pty census entirely); `~` on the call (t_tilde, the lexical limit); e10 -- the comment filter drops every PHYSICAL line beginning with `#`, so code after a closing triple quote or in an f-string field, or a whole file saved with CR-only line endings, escapes (the census F4 pass, the Opus seat).  And the deriver&#x27;s writers are not ATOMIC: a write that fails part-way (a full disk) leaves the gate truncated -- reported since F6e as DERIVE_FAIL rc 6 (controls_c6e t_dfwrite, t_dfgrand); a temporary beside the gate and a rename would keep the old one.  Ranked below live defects: the census guards spellings, not readiness.</span><span class="tip">gate_hygiene.sh&#x27;s readiness census is a SPELLING census.  The census round (#546, pass 2 -&gt; F6e) rebuilt its POSITIVE classifications on Python tokens (regress/census_tokens.py: a comment, a string or a docstring is not code; statement boundaries kept; per-occurrence counts), which closed the comment / string / docstring and most spacing evasions pass 2 and F2 measured.  STILL OPEN, each measured passing all 12 readiness rows on the shipped F6e (regress/artifacts/hygienecensus_20260923/controls_c6e/TABLE.txt, the F2 suite): e9, RANKED FIRST -- the TEXTUAL counts are LINE-based and key on `endswith(`, so a space before the paren (`buf.endswith (&quot;&gt;&quot;)`, the #37 bare defect behind one space) or a backslash continuation (t_bsl) removes a call from all of them; another receiver name (e_e1, n3h); `strip()` or `rstrip(&quot;\r\n&quot;)` for `rstrip()` (e_e5, n3f); a slice compare (e_e4; n10, `buf.rstrip()[-1:] == &quot;&gt;&quot;`, the bare defect again); a parenthesised receiver (n3b, n3c); a regex readiness test (n3i); readiness moved into a helper module (n3k, n3k2 -- no count sees WHICH probe a helper serves); a probe forking with `forkpty` (n4a -- outside the pty census entirely); `~` on the call (t_tilde, the lexical limit); e10 -- the comment filter drops every PHYSICAL line beginning with `#`, so code after a closing triple quote or in an f-string field, or a whole file saved with CR-only line endings, escapes (the census F4 pass, the Opus seat).  And the deriver&#x27;s writers are not ATOMIC: a write that fails part-way (a full disk) leaves the gate truncated -- reported since F6e as DERIVE_FAIL rc 6 (controls_c6e t_dfwrite, t_dfgrand); a temporary beside the gate and a rename would keep the old one.  Ranked below live defects: the census guards spellings, not readiness.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from the census round&#x27;s review passes (pass 2 through F6e&#x27;s controls) -- see the row title for each finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><t