ap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">hygienecensusexotic</span><span class="ttl">tools/derive_hygiene_pins.sh inputs that only a CRAFTED name, a deliberately broken interpreter or a hand-edited gate produce -- FILED, not fixed, by owner ruling (2026-09-23: one more review pass, then file; fix only what a real probe name or real git-bash/WSL use can trigger).  (1) A whole-buffer file name whose space-split pieces each read as a real entry (`arm_bdt_probe.py:9 x.py` beside a real `x.py`) is written, EXPECT_WHOLE_FULL=14 for 5 real sites, every row green (grok, the F5 pass; controls_c6e t_wfcolon3) -- validating the TREE&#x27;s names before the census serialises them closes it.  (2) PYTHONOPTIMIZE drops the writers&#x27; assert checks (codex, the F5 pass; t_pyopt1).  (3) A classifier that dies part-way, or misclassifies, passes the canary -- a liveness check -- so the REPORT, and a --write that carries a ruling, stay unproven against it (the Opus seat&#x27;s S14: a ruled write took EXPECT_WHOLE_FULL to 0 with the gate green).  (4) The reader and the writers key on different layouts of a hand-edited gate (the numeric writers replace the FIRST `^NAME=` line, the running gate uses the LAST).  (5) The gate&#x27;s own GRANDFATHERED_PROMPTLESS body is `eval`&#x27;d before any check (clean today: t_gpbytes).  (6) ANY `.endswith(...)` call is credited as readiness, by the census and the parser alike (glm, the F6 pass).  (7) A census/parser disagreement -- a `match` class pattern -- has no tool exit; the probe must be edited (kimi-k3:cloud, the F6 pass; t_k14release).  (8) The gate&#x27;s `whole_full=$(printf ... $whole_files | awk ...)` expands `$whole_files` unquoted (grok, the F6 pass; no real token holds a glob character, and NTFS forbids `*` and `?`).  Evidence: regress/artifacts/hygienecensus_20260923/controls_c6b/, controls_c6d/, controls_c6e/.</span><span class="tip">tools/derive_hygiene_pins.sh inputs that only a CRAFTED name, a deliberately broken interpreter or a hand-