 &amp; 31)` before their decline guards || ppccrlogicshift -- seven CR logical handlers evaluate signed `1 &lt;&lt; (31-bt)`; bt=0 gives 1&lt;&lt;31 || badfmtlatchrow -- #279&#x27;s two one-shot latches have no committed row that fires them || ftrvfourstores -- only the fr0 store of `ftrv`&#x27;s four is observed (sh_rounding_probe.py:94-98) || mipscvtsdlive -- AMENDED (Astra): the gap is the `cvt.s.d` RN/RZ CONTRAST specifically; the nearest-mode single-store wiring IS observed live (mips_rounding_probe.py:63, the `cvt.s.l`... || testmipshighramrow -- nothing at HEAD observes testmips&#x27;s &gt;256 MB mirror/high mapping (#120&#x27;s &quot;regression-gated&quot; has no carrier; every `-M` under regress/ is 32 or 64) || gberesizezero -- GBE keeps a rejected VCMAP/HCMAP dimension in xres/yres and reads it back through negative shifts || vgacursoronly -- VGA headless console: the OB-16 guard returns before the cursor-only tick can reposition the terminal cursor || pxdmatail -- PX COPYSPANS decodes span records past the bytes the bounded SRAM copy filled || gifputcharovf -- ps2_gif putchar: (24 + y*xsize)*4 overflows int before #108&#x27;s bound; residual of the RESOLVED OB-28 || pxfilladd -- PX fill: int32_t lw + 1 overflows at INT32_MAX before the row loop || lunaintshift -- luna88k: signed 1 &lt;&lt; 31 in the INT_ST_MASK read loop and the line-6 assert/deassert, and highestCurrentStatus &lt;&lt; 29 for levels 4-6 || kn02banameshift -- kn02ba: 1 &lt;&lt; i for i == 31 in the interrupt-name snprintf, the sibling #24 cast at :192 did not || macesignedshift -- MACE assert/deassert compute 1 &lt;&lt; line in int; line 31 is registered and undefined || autodevregorder -- diff_autodev_gen.sh&#x27;s ordered rows compare PROTOTYPE lines; the registration loops are a separate scrape no row observes || lunad3diag -- no row observes luna_intmask_probe.py&#x27;s D3 diagnostic (its &quot;kills a narrowed guard&quot; sentence is ambiguous, not false) || fdcdiagrows -- CHANGELOG #20522&#x27;s &quot;asserted rather than assumed&quot; fdc measurement has no committed carrier || fileloaderrows -- (no ECOFF/Mach-O/SREC/Android corpus row; gate_upstream.sh says so itself) || ascaccountrows -- (no committed row asserts NCR_TCL/NCR_TCM/NCRSTAT_TC) || cuemapgap -- (#127&#x27;s &quot;each regression-gated&quot; CUE claims have no carrier; diff_diskimage_io.c routes reads away from the CUE path) || modeselectrow -- (no diff_diskimage_*.c row issues opcode 0x15) || scsicaprow -- (diff_diskimage_parse.c asserts the PARSER&#x27;s count, never READ CAPACITY -- which is how `drecalccap` shipped past &quot;advertised blocks exact&quot;; discharged by... || m88ktrapmask -- tb0/tb1 build their bit mask with a signed 1 &lt;&lt; d (undefined at d = 31); m88k_rot&#x27;s (1 &lt;&lt; n) - 1 is the same class || mipslowrefrow -- no committed row observes #278&#x27;s `LOW reference` diagnostic (cpu_mips.c:2003, :2029-2037); the CHANGELOG&#x27;s `Probe, 36/36 checks` names two test-first probe rigs that are not in the tree || mipsaddiuub -- ADDIU and seven addition sites across six fused handlers add two int32_t in signed arithmetic (UB on the wrap ADDIU is defined to perform) || mipsjregionub -- MODE32 J/JAL/JAL_trace: `page_base + (int32_t)arg[1]` overflows `int32_t` for a jump in the last two slots of page 0x7ffff000 || leregrows -- the LANCE observations the CHANGELOG cites (CHANGELOG.md:20714 at 7440e129: la_extra_reject, the #274 and #275 probes -- MISS, rmd1, tmd1, tmd3, CSR0) have no committed carrier: no regress file names the device || pvrofssignedovf -- PVR fb tick: `int vram_ofs` (DIWADDRL + y1*bytes_per_line, then per line) can overflow signed int BEFORE the unsigned % VRAM_SIZE -- undefined behaviour; the index is still masked, no out-of-bounds access shown || pvrrgbuninit -- PVR TA: `wf_r/g/b[4]` are not zero-initialised (#12 covered x/y/z/u/v only); a textured strip&#x27;s slide at :1407/:1411 copies indeterminate values || pvrpaletteend -- PVR texture sampler: the #55 clamp `addr &gt; VRAM_SIZE-2` is sized for two-byte texels; it redirects the one legal one-byte sample at VRAM_SIZE-1 (8-bit palette, format... || ppcmixedfx -- no row raises a NEW FPSCR cause while a different one is already set, so the per-bit FX latch (cpu_ppc.c:1933-1946) is checked only for one cause repeated || pitonebytelatch -- no PIT latch row programs a single-byte access format, so the one-read latch release (dev_8253.c:259-261) is unobserved || dbgexprambig -- Breakpoint and watchpoint adds treat PARSE_MULTIPLE as success and then read the output || findaddrwrap -- Debugger memory search can wrap its scan address into low addresses || findcountovf -- Debugger search counts matches and unreadable chunks in unbounded signed ints || dbgignorow -- No committed row observes breakpoint ignore-count stops || mipsbpnormrow -- No committed row observes MIPS breakpoint sign-extension of an unextended address || subsysbprow -- No committed row arms a subsystem breakpoint and observes debugger entry || dbglisterow -- No committed row observes the global break-on-ERROR listing after one subsystem is cleared || stepcallfocus -- Changing machine focus leaves step-call running cached untraced handlers || netipurgptr -- TCP reply checksum covers an urgent pointer the reply never stores || netipseqarith -- TCP sequence difference is a signed subtraction before the mismatch reject || netipbcastmask -- Broadcast mask shifts a signed 1 by an accepted prefix || arcseekshift -- ARC Seek retains a signed byte-decoding shift || arcstdinlimit -- ARC stdin Read overflows its signed loop counter at length 2147483647 || irqcmaskshift -- IRQ mask and unmask writes still use a signed 1 shifted by the guest selector || isopathptr -- ISO path-table checks form pointers beyond one-past || shdmteupper -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:8691-8694 at db8b1a33 -- the SH DMAC interrupt loop stops at DMAE (0x6c0) and omits DMTE4-7 (H&#x27;780-H&#x27;7E0), which exist on SH7750R/SH7751R (cpu_sh.c:447-448).  LOW today because nothing in the tree asserts any DMTE; it becomes MED when `sh4dmacintr` lands, and the loop is to be extended in that round || emulmkstempexit -- emul.c:600-603 calls exit(1) when mkstemp fails -- a host temporary-directory failure ends the process || arcpartlba -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:2730-2731 at db8b1a33 -- the ARC partition LBA is multiplied by 512 in signed int and overflows (arcbios.c:1010-1017; it defeats the #168 bound)</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #554 from the Astra review campaign (wave 1, the emulator source).  This row closes when every member is promoted, fixed or dropped; the members&#x27; rulings and evidence are in regress/artifacts/astraretro_20260926/DISPOSITIONS.md and regress/artifacts/astrafiling_20261002/FILING.tsv.  NOT FIXED by #554.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span