r class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #556.  A correction that sits in a string the program prints is a code change a gate may read, not a records one; one without a replacement sentence needs the sentence written and ruled; one in a file that carries unreviewed working deltas waits for that file; one was not located.  This row closes when every member is made or dropped.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armusrstop</span><span class="ttl">cpu_arm_instr.c: a USER/SYSTEM-mode guest stops the CPU -- LDM {..pc}^ (arm_pop) and MSR SPSR_x (msr_imm_spsr) in USR32/SYS32 reach default: arms that set running = 0 (stops the current CPU; emulation ends when no CPU runs)</span><span class="tip">cpu_arm_instr.c: a USER/SYSTEM-mode guest stops the CPU -- LDM {..pc}^ (arm_pop) and MSR SPSR_x (msr_imm_spsr) in USR32/SYS32 reach default: arms that set running = 0 (stops the current CPU; emulation ends when no CPU runs) — note: filed 2026-10-07 from the Opus 5.5 seat&#x27;s pass-1 answer on armmsrmodekill (F2 disposition 12; owner ruling 2026-10-07: FILE as its own row, not fixed in #562).  USR/SYS have no SPSR, so the architecture makes these UNPREDICTABLE; stopping the CPU is not a permitted outcome (DDI 0100I glossary: must not halt or hang).  Not yet witnessed on HEAD by a rung-3 probe.  Evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/witness_20261007/opus_pass1.md.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armspsrthumb</span><span class="ttl">cpu_arm: an SPSR restore (LDM {..pc}^, DPI S-to-PC) that sets T keeps decoding ARM words until the dyntrans run loop is next entered -- the Thumb interpreter is chosen only at loop entry, arm_pop never breaks out and word-aligns the PC</span><span class="tip">cpu_arm: an SPSR restore (LDM {..pc}^, DPI S-to-PC) that sets T keeps decoding ARM words until the dyntrans run loop is next entered -- the Thumb interpreter is chosen only at loop entry, arm_pop never breaks out and word-aligns the PC — note: filed 2026-10-07 by owner ruling, from #562&#x27;s §F2 pass (codex disposition 6: &#x27;Mode filtering alone does not make applying T safe or coherent&#x27;).  CORRECTED 2026-10-08 by reading the source before the round&#x27;s records were written: the first filing said a restored T=1 &#x27;is not honoured&#x27; -- it IS, but late.  cpu_dyntrans.c picks arm_cpu_interpret_thumb_SLOW only at the run function&#x27;s ENTRY (`if (cpu-&gt;cd.arm.cpsr &amp; ARM_FLAG_T)`); the DPI restore breaks out (abortdyntrans_call) only for an ODD destination PC; arm_pop never breaks out and loads the PC as r[ARM_PC] &amp; 0xfffffffc, dropping bit 1 of a Thumb address.  So after a restore that sets T the CPU can keep decoding ARM words until the loop is next entered.  Out of #562&#x27;s scope (#562 declines only M[4:0]; its probe&#x27;s `tbit&#x27; row pins the T BIT&#x27;s provenance, not the decoder).  Not witnessed; the round owes a rung-3 attempt first.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armmmuvehicle</span><span class="ttl">regress: an ARM rung-3 probe vehicle that runs a guest with the MMU ON (testarm, debugger-driven) -- the reopen condition of armthumbabortkill and the likely vehicle for armdesc3kill / armdacr2kill</span><span class="tip">regress: an ARM rung-3 probe vehicle that runs a guest with the MMU ON (testarm, debugger-driven) -- the reopen condition of armthumbabortkill and the likely vehicle for armdesc3kill / armdacr2kill — note: filed 2026-10-07 by owner ruling: after #562, build this FIRST, then armthumbabortkill.  Open questions: does testarm&#x27;s default CPU (SA1110, ARMv4) support Thumb, or is another -C cpu needed; page-table setup in guest RAM via debugger writes; translation-fault liveness control.  Test-apparatus round (witness kind harness:).  2026-10-08 agy READING (regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/agy_research_20261008.txt; facts to re-derive, not agreement): testarm default CPU SA1110; NO per-CPU Thumb capability flag -- the T bit alone selects arm_cpu_interpret_thumb_SLOW, so any -C runs Thumb; CP15 c1/c2/c3 are NOT debugger-settable -&gt; the guest must mcr them; `put&#x27; writes VIRTUAL memory; `step&#x27; keeps working with the MMU on; minimal map = one section descriptor 0x00000c02 at a 16 KB-aligned TTB, DACR 1.  THE VEHICLE MUST MAP THE EXCEPTION VECTORS or a fault reaches cpu_dyntrans.c&#x27;s &#x27;could not find physical address of the exception handler&#x27; exit (tracked as alphaifetchkill).  Of the exits and stops agy listed on this path, these match existing rows by title: armdesc3kill, armdacr2kill, armcp15cp14exits, armendianexit, qharmexalign, alphaifetchkill.  NOT complete, and two entries were wrong as given (GPT-6 Astra, #562&#x27;s confirmation): armsa1110areset is the reset alignment-control default, not the ARM_EXCEPTION_RESET exit agy listed (that exit may be unfiled), and agy&#x27;s &#x27;wfi&#x27; stop in cpu_arm_instr.c is X(reboot).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><sp