pan class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — REAL — drive_guest.py:197-199 hardcodes /tmp/gxregress; LOGDIR never read; gate_hygiene grades $LOGDIR/drive_*.log — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/kimi_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — REAL — but honoring $LOGDIR alone is insufficient without a caller change too — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/glm_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — UNKNOWN — UNKNOWN — cannot read file:line; hardcoded /tmp/gxregress is plausible but unverified. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/deepseek_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — REAL — a configurable log path that the script silently ignores is a test-isolation bug. (packet-only resend after the mixed-brief stall; P3 resolved) — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/assess/minimax_resend_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export at lib.sh:24 + os.environ.get at :197-199, ONE carrier shared by producer and grader. Rejects argv (a SECOND carrier - writer and grader could diverge) and a call-site prefix (the census must then remember it, and forgetting is silently inert - the defect class under repair). DETECTOR TRAP NAMED: do NOT use `env LOGDIR=...`, which exports from outside and stays green with lib.sh&#x27;s export missing - that tests half the defect. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_dispatches/fable5_r1_n5_n6_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — export at lib.sh:24 AND `os.environ.get(&quot;LOGDIR&quot;) or &quot;/tmp/gxregress&quot;` at :197 - MEASURED, the or-form is REQUIRED: the .get(default) form that the other eight seats proposed writes to the FILESYSTEM ROOT when LOGDIR is empty. Also measured: the driver-only fix is CONDITIONALLY inert (dead for `LOGDIR=x; ./run.sh`, live for an exported value) - worse than uniform. A GATE-5 ROW IS MEASURED VACUOUS (in the default battery LOGDIR equals the hardcoded literal); the detector must be an offline selftest with a private LOGDIR and a synthetic rig name, asserting the FILES not the driver&#x27;s LOG= line (a half-fix kept LOG= correct while the raw log escaped). — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_dispatches/opus_r1_research_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR from lib.sh and derive both driver log paths from it. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/codex_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR in lib.sh; driver reads os.environ.get with the same default. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/agy_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export LOGDIR from lib.sh; the driver joins that directory for both pty logs. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/grok_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — MANUAL — export at lib.sh:24 AND os.environ.get at :197-199, proven by a fake-emulator selftest wired into gate_offline.sh (a new selftest_logdir.py, not a gate-5 row). — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/kimi_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export at lib.sh:25 + os.environ.get at :196-199. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/glm_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export LOGDIR; driver reads it with the /tmp/gxregress default. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/deepseek_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — BELIEVED — packet: export in lib.sh; resolve both pty paths via os.environ.get. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/d1/research/minimax_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c hold"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">⏸</span><span class="tip">2026-08-15 — CONFIRMED — Implemented and committed as f92e5a1 with its detector. Gate 2 PASS (122 checks) including the two new rows; the detector was negative-controlled in BOTH directions - no/no FAIL on the unfixed tree before the edit, yes/yes PASS after. Awaiting the panel&#x27;s review of the actual diff. — evidence: pipeline/evidence/_closure/r1_research_closure_2026-08-15.md</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-20 — CONFIRMED — CLOSED AS ALREADY-COMPLETE, and verified before closing rather than taken from the hold. Nobody proposed dropping these -- the adjudicator found them while asked what should be closed that no seat had raised, and its point stands: FINISHED WORK HAD SAT OPEN FOR FIVE DAYS.
.\tools\pipeline\matrix.html:21763:repair 14 FULLY STAGED -- probe edits, contract, PRETABLE, check_pred.py, mutants_r14.py and a map-verified 15-leg driver, all ordered before any run. Three checkers green. NOTHING MEASURED; #530 table 7 still holds the machine, deliberately unraced. Next: fire table 12, then the INTMASK/CONTROL-write swaps Fable requires MEASURED, then the decline carriers</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 13a (the INTMASK and CONTROL-write label swaps the stop condition required MEASURED): CHECK13A_PASS -- base 204/204, M7_intmasklatch 201/204, M8_ctllatch 201/204, each exact against PRETABLE13a.out.  No INTMASK or CONTROL carrier owed.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 14 (repair 15: the TIME and REV decline carriers, the entries 13-and-17 pair): CHECK14_PASS, 18 legs exact -- base 218/218 on probe f5e915f6; M3_timelatch and M5_revlatch 214/218 (were 204/204 escapes); M6/M7/M8 215/218; D_nodogclear 216/218.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 15a (pass 2&#x27;s finding): H_noresetclear and E_noendianclear 218/218, both escapes AS PREDICTED -- the HARD_RESET clear&#x27;s residue had no row; ENDIANESS disclosed.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 16 (repair 16: the CONTROL arm&#x27;s residue-text count for each clear in both latch states): CHECK16_PASS, 25/25 legs exact on probe 5f770991 (226 rows) -- H_noresetclear and E_noendianclear now detected; W_istlb and W_imklb 226/226 as predicted (disclosed).  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — [EVIDENCE REPAIRED 2026-09-26 by #529: this entry cited `_scratchpad/fable_flagship_20260918.md (brief)`, a volatile brief, while the answer lived only in the transcript -- 87 claude-fable-5-1 turns, 0 refusals, a genuine seat answer.]  **RATIFY** the panel&#x27;s refutation of P2/P3 and the reshaped repair 14; **DISSENT on closure readiness -- two checkable defects sit in the working tree and ONE WOULD RED THE GATE TODAY.**  VERIFIED: `regress/gate_arm.sh`&#x27;s uncommitted hunk pins `crime_width rows run` at **188**, while every repair-14 leg since 09-17 08:34 reads **/204** -- a gate run on this tree reds three checks.  The pin must move to 204 in the same commit as the probe, AFTER the base leg (the `#462` rule).  VERIFIED: there is no `#529` commit at all, and `regress/crime_width_probe.py` is staged `A` but never committed; table 12 was aborted at leg 4 of 15 and re-fired, so the ruling&#x27;s own stop condition -- every enumerated mutant built and killed, the zero carried with its denominator -- is NOT met until that table completes. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/flagship_20260918/fable5_flagship_20260918_answer.txt (the answer, extracted from transcript agent-a2865c082138f4cf6; its brief beside it)</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1-MEASURED-DESIGN-INVALID</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** VERDICT: DO NOT SHIP REPAIR 14 AS PROPOSED.  P2 IS FALSE AND P3 IS FALSE, AND IT MEASURED BOTH. SIX MUTANTS, TWO TABLES, PREDICTIONS MATCHED 6 OF 6. *** base 188/188 | PC_imk4r 187/188 reds `gate line&#x27; (POSITIVE CONTROL, reproducing close-8 exactly) | M1_gotolatch 178/188 KILLED on ten rows | **M2_ld278clr 188/188 ESCAPE** | M4_timeplain 184/188 (DISCRIMINATING CONTROL, exactly the four predicted rows) | **M3_timelatch 188/188 TOTAL ESCAPE**. **O1, THE FINDING OF THE ROUND: THE 56-CELL PRODUCT IS THE ACCEPT HALF OF A 112-CELL SPACE.**  It describes only accesses that are SERVICED.  The DECLINE arm -- the thing #529 ADDED -- has its own product {len 1,2} x {R,W} x {7 labels} x {latch}, and the enumeration contains NONE of it.  **Parts A and B are both accept-side, so NEITHER CAN REACH IT.**  This supersedes the deepseek-vs-codex disagreement entirely: they were arguing how to extend the accept-side product while the missing half was a different arm of the same `if&#x27;. **O2: P3 IS FALSE -- THE K-FORM IS LOUD, NOT SILENT.**  It falls into the decline arm, SETS the latch and PRINTS; it escapes because the announce is STOLEN (in `latch x5&#x27;&#x27;s prologue the count stays 1), not because it is absent.  The G-form is the silent one.  **My brief reasoned `it declines silently&#x27; and aimed the repair at value oracles -- reasoning from silence pointed the repair at the wrong channel.** **O3, the Q2 answer, MEASURED: a TWO-LINE edit scores 188/188** -- move `goto crime_declined&#x27; INSIDE the latch block and condition it on `relative_addr != CRIME_TIME&#x27;.  A narrow access at CRIME_TIME that is NOT its session&#x27;s first refusal falls into the switch and advances the guest clock, one of the four defects the fix&#x27;s own comment says the goto prevents.  The SAME edit without the latch conjunct (M4_timeplain) is killed 184/188 on exactly the four predicted rows -- ~2.2 million to one on the raw value -- and the liveness control reads `large&#x27; in BOTH runs, so the channel is live and the difference is the mutant.  **Part A cannot test this at all: a pre-latch session by construction contains no refusal before the cell under test.** **O4: the decline x latch-SET axis derived -- 7 cells, 2 OPEN (REV and TIME)**, on a discriminator that needs no run (does any session refuse at this label more than ONCE?).  *** AND THE PROBE ALREADY KNEW: crime_width_probe.py:1077-1079 states the asymmetry in as many words, derived for a DIFFERENT mutant, and nobody turned it around to ask what it implies for the goto. ***  Two rows in one diff close the axis. **O5: M2_ld278clr is a FIFTH escape and it CONFIRMS my buckets re-derivation independently** -- ACCEPTS entry 46 (ld +0x278) is one of the eight PRE-BLIND entries buckets8.py named, and the only one with neither an equivalence derivation nor a measurement.  The seat reached it by BUILDING A MUTANT; the deriver reached it by READING SESSIONS.  Two roads, same cell. **O6: Part A&#x27;s denominator is 8, not 23** (mirror14.py: N_ENTRIES_WITH_NO_PRELATCH_OBSERVER=8 of 46) -- matching BUCKETS8_rerun.out&#x27;s N_PRE_BLIND=8 exactly, from an independent tool. **O7: Q3 IS UNANSWERABLE AS POSED AND THE PROBE&#x27;S OWN HEADER SAYS SO** -- 2 of the 5 HOST-DIAGNOSTIC and 6 of the 10 EQUIVALENT cells have NO LISTED MEMBERS (crime_width_probe.py:242-257: `a bucket whose members cannot be listed cannot be audited&#x27;).  My brief promoted those counts to a SETTLED PREMISE while its own source flags them unlistable.  **8 of 46 cannot be checked by anyone**, so the nine-entry demand is a FLOOR rather than the answer. O8: four unnamed axes collapse with warrants (cpu-&gt;is_32bit is DEAD CODE on ip32 -- subtype 32 -&gt; R4400 -&gt; isa_level 3 -&gt; is_32bit == 0; ncpus; use_fb; physical_ram_in_mb).  **A DOMAIN DEPENDENCY NOBODY HAD STATED:** a real MIPS guest emits len in {1,2,4,8} exactly, but memory_rw.c:495-523 CLAMPS len at a device&#x27;s end and can emit 1..7 -- inert here ONLY because DEV_CRIME_LENGTH is 0x280, a multiple of 8.  That makes codex&#x27;s reachability argument conditional on a constant rather than absolute.  Also: an accepted HARD_RESET write TERMINATES its session, so Part B costs one NEW SESSION per cell; and #529&#x27;s own diff created a stale citation -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:5574 cites dev_sgi_ip32.c:698, now :728. O9, ITS OWN ERRORS RECORDED BY THE SEAT RATHER THAN BY ME: a row-to-session off-by-one in its deriver (found pre-ship; buckets8.py unaffected), the backslash trap twice, and **a CRLF script that EXITED 0 HAVING BUILT AND RUN NOTHING** -- caught only because two seconds is impossible for two 17-minute probes.  No damage: the cd failed before the sentinel was dropped. FOOTPRINT CLEAN: no project tree written, all four fork copies still md5 8c1d1545..., clone sentinel cleared, source cmp-clean, binary -nt source, restored byte-identical to base. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/opus_pass1.md (30 KB) and opus_pass1_work/ -- PREDICT.md 23:58:36 and PREDICT2.md 00:04:17 against builds at 00:00:0x / 00:18:4x; six probe logs all ending CRIMEP_DONE; mirror14.py, mutants14.py, frozen drivers kill14.run-000006.sh / kill14b.run-001836.sh</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1-REFIRE-ANSWERED</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — MANUAL — *** THE RE-FIRE WORKED: 353 KB streamed, ZERO content-filter flags, 7,826 b of verdict.  SAME SEAT, SAME QUESTIONS, SAME TREE -- only neutral vocabulary, reading scoped to src/ + regress/*.py, and the edit-construction question dropped.  The section-C5 remedy is validated a second time, on the seat it was minted from. ***  VERDICT: repair 14 needs a revised coverage model.  **ITS DEEPEST FINDING REFRAMES THE DOMAIN AND CUTS AGAINST THE OTHER SEATS&#x27; REMEDY**: adding lane and PROM-window state mechanically gives 224 nominal tuples, but that MISREPRESENTS REACHABILITY -- the MIPS producer checks natural alignment and the CRIME switch matches the EXACT offset, so every named label has the lane bit CLEAR and a 4-byte access to a register&#x27;s low lane reaches `default&#x27;.  The lane is NOT a free factor, so the corrected enumeration is REACHABILITY-CONSTRAINED rather than a cross-product -- meaning deepseek&#x27;s remedy (state the six-factor product) would have been wrong in the opposite direction.  Two seats pushed the enumeration opposite ways and the truth is neither.  **A RECORDS FINDING NO OTHER SEAT REACHED:** the shipped probe has NO direct value assertion for accepted CONTROL `lw +0x08&#x27; -- it runs through ACCEPTS where its destination is overwritten, `devsig hi&#x27; checks REV and `acc ctl ld&#x27; checks EIGHT-byte CONTROL -- so the equivalence derivation is sound but its claimed supporting row is missing.  That independently confirms the close-8 reading that table 11&#x27;s C_ctl4r leg was vacuous for want of an ORACLE rather than an ACCESS.  Also named four arms whose effects the common tail does NOT reproduce (DOG&#x27;s register effects, INTSTAT&#x27;s interrupt-LINE update, TIME&#x27;s update, REV&#x27;s PC effect), and independently enumerated the instrument at 51 sessions / 188 uniquely named rows -- a free cross-check on the denominator every score in this campaign is quoted against. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">2026-09-16 — MANUAL — GO-WITH-CHANGES.  **FOUND F3, AND IT REFUTES A CLAIM OF MINE USING THE PROBE&#x27;S OWN HEADER.**  My brief said an early `return&#x27; in place of `goto crime_declined&#x27; would skip the interrupt recomputation and memory_writemax64, &#x27;a defect the shipped code does not have&#x27;.  crime_width_probe.py:269-272 says the opposite and gives the warrant: the two are EQUIVALENT on every channel because memory_rw pre-zeroes a device read buffer (#95) and nothing on a declined access writes HARDINT or SOFTINT, so the tail&#x27;s restore and recompute are identities -- measured 40/40 in kill table 1 and formally DISCLOSED.  UPHELD: the statements are mechanically skipped and the skipping is UNOBSERVABLE, so the consequence I attached is what is false.  I imported a correct general caution (the four-readers common-tail lesson) into the one site where it had been measured not to apply. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — MANUAL — NOT RATIFIED as written -- and the strongest answer of the panel.  It reached the 46-vs-56 finding INDEPENDENTLY and supplied the MECHANISM no other seat did: 23 is a count of ACCEPTS ENTRIES rowed post-latch by repair 13, not of product cells, and MANY ENTRIES MAP TO ONE CELL (the CONTROL writes 0x0201 / 0x0001 / 0 / 0x0200 / 0x0100 are five entries of ONE cell), which is why no re-count could ever reconcile 46 with 56.  **IT THEN DERIVED WHY INTSTAT 4R ESCAPES EVERYTHING**: using 23 as the class-closure denominator is how IST 4R falls through -- it is not in the 23 because the SET side is already pinned by `istat ctl&#x27;, and it is still open on CLEAR.  **THE MISSING FLOOR CELL, NAMED WITH ITS ORACLE REQUIREMENT: INTSTAT 4R, latch-CLEAR, with SOFTINT|HARDINT SEEDED NONZERO** -- sharper than my own criterion, which said `driven pre-refusal with an oracle&#x27; and did not say what the oracle must contain.  ADDS A DESIGN CONSTRAINT I had not stated: G_clr_imk4r 187/188 reddening `gate line&#x27; must STAY the positive control in the 188-row instrument, so the next closing pass keeps a CLEAR-half control that is not TIME -- repair 14 owes a check that it does not disturb it.  ALSO: P1 was NOT the full enclosing function; the omitted prelude at 229-235 (CONTROL = ENDIANESS 0x100 on every access) IS the warrant for the CONTROL-4R equivalence the packet asserted without it.  A section-D violation of mine. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **VERDICT: DO NOT RATIFY AS WRITTEN.**  *** AN UNREAD REVIEW ON AN IN-FLIGHT ROUND, RECORDED 2026-09-17 -- it answered on 2026-09-16 and had no cell until section G surfaced it. ***  Transport: `kimi-k3:cloud` SUBSTITUTE, so PACKET-FED; its claims are the packet&#x27;s, walked rather than re-derived from the tree. **IT WALKED THE ARITHMETIC RATHER THAN REASONING ABOUT IT, which is what the brief asked for and what makes its finding checkable:** `2x2x2x7 = 56` (seven case labels, six named plus `default`); `23 + 8 + 10 + 5 = 46`; *** therefore **56 - 46 = 10 CELLS APPEAR IN NO CATEGORY** ***.  It names the settling fact rather than guessing at the cause -- *the per-cell disposition table* -- and says plainly that the ACCEPTS-to-cell map is not settleable from the packet. **FINDING 1 -- THE PACKET CONTRADICTS ITSELF:** P4 claims *&quot;the latch-CLEAR state is driven by session 40 (`latch x5`) ALONE&quot;*, and P5&#x27;s own positive control disproves it -- `G_clr_imk4r` is killed at 187/188 and the brief itself assigns that kill to session 20. **It also re-checked three claims by walking the bit operations:** the 0x800-clear claim (`0x01 &amp; 0x800 = 0`, `0x0001 &amp; 0x800 = 0`, `0x0201 &amp; 0x800 = 0`), noting that 0x0201 also carries 0x200 set so that bit IS driven both ways post-latch; and both mutant row counts (`t4clear.py` 5-3 = 2 red rows with exactly two named; `ctlreset.py` each K mutant single-reds its own row). *Fourth unread review today to carry a real finding.  This one is a COVERAGE gap with its denominator on a round still in flight.* — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/ollama_kimi.txt 12529 b</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">2026-09-16 — MANUAL — NOT CLEAN.  **FOUND F2 -- the packet&#x27;s own internal contradiction, from the packet alone.**  P4 says the latch-CLEAR state is driven by session 40 ALONE; P5 says G_clr_imk4r, a latch-CLEAR conjunct, is KILLED 187/188.  A latch-SET row cannot red a latch-CLEAR mutant -- the conjunct is inert once the latch is set -- so one of the two is mis-stated.  It NAMED THE SETTLING FACT rather than picking a side.  Also found F1 (the 46-vs-56 gap).  SETTLED IN MY FAVOUR OF NEITHER: the gate-run session calls POST() nowhere and drives INTMASK 4R at :735 BEFORE its first refusal at :741, so P4&#x27;s ALONE is FALSE. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">2026-09-16 — MANUAL — REJECT REPAIR AS SCOPED.  **FOUND F6:** the brief states the domain as a four-factor 56-cell product and then names two FURTHER factors of the same handler (relative_addr &amp; 4, cpu-&gt;pc) as &#x27;measured closed&#x27;.  If they partition the handler they are factors, so the domain is at least 2x56.  Calling them closed while excluding them from the arithmetic is an omission with a note attached, not a disclosure.  UPHELD -- and it is the strongest kind of catch, needing no repo access to see that the brief contradicted itself. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">2026-09-16 — MANUAL — BRIEF HAS REAL DEFECTS.  **FOUND F5:** P6 says the CONTROL arm tests DOG 0x200, HARD_RESET 0x800 &#x27;and the leftover&#x27;, while P1 inlines only the case LABELS -- thirty lines of CONTROL body unaccounted for, so Part B may be narrower than the generating-set clause demands.  UPHELD; inline 353-382 before pass 2.  ALSO ASKED F4, the right question against an elided region: does CRIME_HARDINT (0x020) have its own case in the un-inlined 385-387?  **CHECKED: NO** -- 385-387 is the shared body of the INTSTAT/INTMASK fall-through pair, so HARDINT falls to default and the seven-label count stands.  The premise survived the audit, which is the audit working. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-26 — THE CHAIN CLOSES ON THIS PASS — #529 repair 16&#x27;s F2 pass: the FLAGSHIP seat, LAST (claude-fable-5-1 by agent_models.py; one mid-run refusal event, recovered on the same model -- the answer and the final text are fable-5-1).  Verbatim: &quot;THE CHAIN CLOSES ON THIS PASS -- zero floor breaches survive adjudication on a valid, full-roster pass; repair 16&#x27;s rows all stand; NO row is owed.&quot;  X1 and X3 graded clause (e); its Q3 items 1-12 applied as r17, item 13&#x27;s records outside the probe landing with #529&#x27;s commit, r18 adding GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s r17 audit and the ACCEPTS-46 enumeration, r19 one docstring sentence from Astra&#x27;s second records audit (2026-09-28), and r20 the final ruling&#x27;s comment correction at ACCEPTS entry 21 plus the MEASURED/derived qualifier (2026-09-30), r21 the four text fixes of Astra&#x27;s confirmation of that ruling, and r22 one docstring qualifier the precommit hook&#x27;s score-claim check required (the committed text). — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair16_f2_20260926/fable5_f2_adjudication.md — record: 2026-09-14 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: MEASURED from the subagent transcri