so nothing is new but the enumeration SOURCE.  Bounded to the labels of the ONE skipped dispatch in the enclosing function.  **And it carries its own expiry: minted from one device, so its first reuse elsewhere should CHECK the enumeration, not merely obey it** -- the freshly-minted-exemplar rule applied by the seat to its own ruling. Q4: upholds every reversal the panel forced (O1/112 withdrawn, O2&#x27;s redirect withdrawn, A11 vacuous, A13 self-applied to 1-of-2); keeps D1 OPEN as a CONDITION rather than a number; and **reverses NOTHING in the fix direction -- the goto de-fatalisation itself is unchallenged across two passes, and the entire dispute is detector coverage.** ORDER: (1) entry 14, sharpest and cheapest L2; (2) decline closure = TIME + REV carriers PLUS the INTMASK/CONTROL-write swap VERIFICATION; (3) accept closure = 21x2 seeded, 32/33, 46; (4) A11-&gt;A12 pair; (5) 13/17 after the CHANNEL check; (6) FILE A9&#x27;s kills, D1&#x27;s split-width routing, and the +2 translation. — record: 2026-09-17 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: this verification rested on the answer&#x27;s own `MODEL: claude-fable-5-1&#x27; line -- a SELF-REPORT, a check that cannot fail.  The subagent transcript (per-message `model&#x27; and `stop_reason&#x27;; _scratchpad/agent_models.py) shows the file was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 at 06:25:19Z (agent a2bba4bc2896433b4), after claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot; at 2026-09-17T06:17:21Z.  The first-hand ruling is regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md (the first-hand fable5 ruling of 2026-09-25, entered below; it re-anchors C3, D7, Q3 and STOP). ***  *** SEAT VERIFIED AS FABLE, PER THE STANDING DIRECTIVE THAT A SUBAGENT CONFIRM FABLE USAGE RATHER THAN OPUS. ***  MODEL line reads `claude-fable-5-1&#x27; VERBATIM; liveness token present; VERDICT LINE FIRST; and the checker was asked explicitly whether the file is an ECHOED PROMPT rather than an answer -- it is not, it answers Q1-Q4 with reasoned dispositions.  That last check exists because this project once scored a 26,992-byte ECHOED BRIEF as the best answer in its panel. *** ONE MISMATCH, AND IT IS MINE, AND IT IS A GENUINE APPARATUS FINDING RATHER THAN A SEAT FAILURE. *** The ruling quotes CHECKPOINT.md&#x27;s first line as `2026-09-16 ~22:2x ...&#x27;; the file now reads `2026-09-17 ~01:2x ...&#x27;.  **I REFRESHED THE CHECKPOINT HEADER WHILE FABLE WAS STILL RUNNING**, so the quote is verbatim-correct for the file AS IT WAS WHEN THE SEAT READ IT, and I invalidated the seat&#x27;s own liveness proof underneath it.  Everything else in the line -- the HEAD stamp 9c91999 and the full trailing text -- matches exactly, which is what shows the seat really read the file. &gt; **THE RULE THIS BUYS: THE FILE-QUOTE LIVENESS CHECK REQUIRES THE QUOTED FILE TO BE STABLE FOR THE DURATION OF THE SEAT&#x27;S RUN.**  The echo test proves prompt delivery AND file access by asking for a verbatim quote -- and it silently stops proving the second half if the quoted file is edited mid-flight.  A mismatch then reads as a DEAD OR HALLUCINATING SEAT when the seat was neither.  Quote a file nothing in the round is going to touch, or freeze the quoted line for the run. *Caught only because the verifying subagent was told IN ADVANCE to distinguish a timestamp-only difference from a real failure -- had it not been, a correct Fable ruling would have been recorded as failing its own liveness check.* — record: 2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] The re-ruling&#x27;s first firing was written by claude-opus-4-8 after a refusal by claude-fable-5-1 (agent_models.py); kept as evidence, relabelled, never counted as the seat. — record: 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] The flagship&#x27;s first answer on repair 15&#x27;s pass 2 was written by claude-opus-4-8 after two refusals by claude-fable-5-1 (agent_models.py); relabelled, never counted as the seat.</span></span></td><td class="c