ccumulated into `tmp&#x27; while the destination is assigned `tmp &amp; tmp2&#x27; and tmp2 is never anything but 0 -- one of the most common 64-bit PowerPC instructions returns 0 for every input</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">cpu_ppc_instr.c X(rldicl) ALWAYS WRITES ZERO: the mask is accumulated into `tmp&#x27; while the destination is assigned `tmp &amp; tmp2&#x27; and tmp2 is never anything but 0 -- one of the most common 64-bit PowerPC instructions returns 0 for every input — commits: e777ff06 — FIXED AND SHIPPED AS #522.  X(rldicl) wrote ZERO to its destination on every execution: the mask was ORed into the ROTATED VALUE while the destination got `tmp &amp; tmp2&#x27; and tmp2 was never anything but 0.  ONE TOKEN fixes it, and it repairs both halves because the `|=&#x27; had also destroyed the rotated data.  This is the canonical 64-bit masking and zero-extension instruction, so it was wrong on the ordinary path for ordinary compiler output.  WITNESSED at rung 3 before the edit, 19/27 -&gt; 24/27, with a 190-cell census in which every cell was wrong and every cell returned exactly zero.  *** PASS 2 RETURNED BREACH-FOUND WITH TWO MEASURED TOTAL ESCAPES, both repaired in-round: a shift-decode mutant the instrument was blind to BY CONSTRUCTION (the census uses an all-ones source, so rotating it is the identity, and the only rotate-sensitive rows drove shifts below 32 while every logical right shift uses 32 or more); and a condition-register mutant that is NOT INVENTED -- it is the token the sibling handler ships correctly ten lines below. ***  Three rows close both, each the sole killer of its mutant, all three also reddening under the defect and the null medium.  FIVE RECORDS were wrong and are corrected, including a citation in PRODUCT CODE and a detector row that cannot fail under any mutation.  The apparatus failed twice and both failures are preserved rather than deleted -- one of them looked HALF-HEALTHY because two mutators share a mutant name.  Two sibling defects in the same family are filed, measured and unfixed; a gate claim of mine was false and is corrected in place. — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/opus_ppc_rldicl_witness_20260910.py -- RUNG 3 on unmodified -E bareppc (and testppc, and macppc -e g5), real instructions through real decode and execution, nothing edited to reach the site.  COMMITTED 19/27 with 190 of 190 census cells wrong and all 190 returning zero; FIX 24/27 with 0 of 190 wrong.  Logs witness_committed.out / witness_fix.out / witness_naive.out, each verified by its PPC_RLDICL_WITNESS_DONE sentinel.  SHIPPED DETECTOR: regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py, 24 rows, killtable_20260910/t2/SCORES.txt -- BASE 24/24, the whole-file PRE-FIX leg 16/24 [clause (a); labelled &#x27;null medium&#x27; until 2026-10-09 -- an L4 per 7n-1; clause (c) is unmeasured and OWED, row nullmediumlegs], EIGHT mutants 16..23/24, ZERO ESCAPES, restore verified on both parts.  The two mutants that escaped the 19-row form (M_SH5, M_CR0) are each killed ONLY by the rows added for them. — note: [2026-10-02] COMMITS FIELD FILLED by #557 from the census of closed rows with no commit (regress/artifacts/closeassess_20261002/grok/grok_closedcensus.txt; Astra&#x27;s git log, regress/artifacts/closeassess_20261002/aconf_census/codex_aconf_census.txt): e777ff06 -- names the row and #522; touches src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c.  </span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></t