  They had their own sentence. **MEASURED OVER EVERY CLUSTER IN THE LEDGER, BOTH KEYS, SAME RUN:**  OLD `note[:60]` -- 64 clusters, 44 genuine, **20 NOTES DIFFER**; NEW full note -- 54 clusters, **54 genuine, 0 notes differ**. *** IT FAILED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, AND THE SECOND HALF IS THE SURPRISE: GENUINE STAMPS ROSE 44 -&gt; 54. ***  A 60-character bucket holding a real stamp ALONGSIDE other notes scored as one mixed cluster, so **the prefix key was HIDING TEN REAL STAMPS BY MERGING THEM**.  Truncation cost recall as well as precision; it never bought either. **ALL SEVEN LIVE REDS WERE FALSE**, each with seven genuinely distinct notes -- so section O was blocking commits on nothing. **CONTROLLED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS:** `BOILERPLATE_PASS` with the seven gone; an INJECTED identical paragraph across four seat cells post-cutoff turns it red and names the row; removing the injection restores green. *** AND A HARNESS BUG OF MINE IS RECORDED IN THE FILE, because it produced a wrong number first: `shared_notes` returns its key with NEWLINES REPLACED BY SPACES for display, so a verification that compares a recomputed key against the RETURNED one silently matches nothing for any note containing a newline -- and then reports the cluster as non-identical. ***  It made one cluster (`wdcnoirq`) look like a survivor when the fix had worked.  *Recompute the bucket; never compare against the display key.*  **Third time this session that a check of mine keyed on a correlate of the thing rather than the thing.** — evidence: tools/pipeline/check_boilerplate.py; 64-cluster two-key census over the ledger</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c hold"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">⏸</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — awaiting fable5 — [HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5] boilerplateprefix closed with commits e1871fa5 (#557 landed its parked check_boilerplate.py repair) and so owes the REGRESS review, a distinct phase under the regress-is-fable-only directive.  Held by #558 (2026-10-02); the Fable agent seat is deliberately not fired (owner instruction, 2026-10-02), so the hold stands for the owner&#x27;s batched flagship sign-off.  The question is in the row&#x27;s hold_question.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">exemptcliff</span><span class="ttl">eleven probe exemptions in check_probe_wiring.py all expire 2026-09-20 -- a deliberate alignment of TWO debts that nine later exemptions copied, so the checker reds on eleven unrelated probes at once</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">eleven probe exemptions in check_probe_wiring.py all expire 2026-09-20 -- a deliberate alignment of TWO debts that nine later exemptions copied, so the checker reds on eleven unrelated probes at once — commits: 04500deb — #550 CLOSES.  The ten exemptions that all fell due 2026-09-27 carry ten dates, 2026-10-08 to 2026-12-03, each with its own reason in owed-work order (owner ruling 2026-09-24); gate 2&#x27;s SC_EXEMPT pair decided separately (ieee_store to 2026-12-10; wdc_identify fixed by #551).  Measured: schedule_v3final.out and the selftest 22/22.  Four panels (pass 1 + F2, pass 2 + F2), the flagship seat LAST on both F2s (SHIP on v3 final); codex walled on every panel, re-fired and Astra&#x27;s confirmation after the 07:01 reset.  Filed: exemptdistinct, asanfifteen.  Badge A: the main loop adjudicated its own round&#x27;s records. — witness: harness:regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/measured/schedule_v3final.out -- the final checker (96efac51) run at each date on a HEAD export: PASS through 2026-10-08, then one problem more per lapsed date, 1 on 10-09 to 10 on 12-04; selftest 22/22 (selftest_550v3final.out) — note: *** STATUS 2026-09-25 (GXEMUL): #550 DISPERSES the block -- ten dates, 2026-10-08 to 2026-12-03, each with its reason (regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/).  CLOSED. ***
.\tools\pipeline\matrix.html:21767:*** ELEVEN PROBE EXEMPTIONS FALL DUE ON THE SAME DAY, 2026-09-20 -- THREE DAYS FROM THIS FILING.  Measured 2026-09-17 by the Opus 5 seat and verified here. ***  A date histogram over `check_probe_wiring.py`&#x27;s `EXEMPT` table: **11 entries dated `2026-09-20`**, plus one `2026-09-19` and one `2026-09-21` -- so **thirteen exemptions expire inside three days**, eleven of them together. *** AND THE PILE-UP IS AN ACCIDENT OF A DELIBERATE CHOICE, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH RECORDING. ***  The file&#x27;s own comment explains the date: *&quot;2026-09-20 matches the fbpending_bound:2026-09-20 deadline already standing in gate_offline.sh&#x27;s SM_EXEMPT, so `#442`&#x27;s two debts fall due together.&quot;*  **Aligning TWO debts was a good idea; nine more have since been written to the same date, and nobody chose that.**  Each new exemption copied the date it found. **WHAT IT COSTS IF NOTHING IS DONE:** on 2026-09-20 the checker reds on eleven probes at once, and a gate that reds on eleven unrelated things is the shape this project already names -- *a rule that retro-fails at scale gets switched off, and a disabled rule is worse than no rule*.  The honest options are to WIRE them, to RE-DATE them individually with their own warrants, or to retire the ones whose rounds are closed -- but **not** to push the whole table forward as one edit, which is how the pile-up formed. *Note one of the eleven is `ppc_rldicl_probe.py`, whose repair is uncommitted and whose row (`ppcwitnessmaskoracle`) is open -- so that debt is about to come due on an oracle nothing executes.*</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-24 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #548 (2026-09-24) discharged one of the eleven 2026-09-27 exemptions (fbpending_drain_probe.py, wired into gate_arm.sh on all four timers, its entry deleted).  TEN remain, all dated 2026-09-27 (derived from the EXEMPT table), so the block still falls due together on 2026-09-28; the owner&#x27;s ruling on that cliff is pending.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 adjudication of pass 1, the FLAGSHIP seat, fired LAST; claude-fable-5-1 throughout by agent_models.py (agent a60d8fda..., clean).  Verdict, verbatim: &quot;#550 VERDICT: SHIP WITH CHANGES&quot; -- deepseek&#x27;s DO NOT SHIP does not stand (the ten re-dates belong to the 2026-09-24 ruling; the 09-25 one decided the SC_EXEMPT pair). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/fable5_f2_550_551.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 pass on pass 1 -- the Opus 5 MEASURING seat (Agent tool; claude-opus-5-5 throughout by agent_models.py, agent a8c6fd47...; every build in a scratch clone, GXEMUL-SEC untouched).  Same model family as the main loop: badge s.  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/opus5_f2.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — DED