gress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_144644/ollama_kimi.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 1 (panel_20260925_144644, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_144644/).  glm (PACKET-FED, glm-5.3:cloud, 5503 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_144644/ollama_glm.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — DO NOT SHIP — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 1 (panel_20260925_144644, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_144644/).  deepseek (PACKET-FED, deepseek-v4-pro:cloud, 760 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: DO NOT SHIP.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_144644/ollama_deepseek.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 1 (panel_20260925_144644, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_144644/).  minimax (PACKET-FED, minimax-m3:cloud, 2760 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_144644/ollama_minimax.txt</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-26 — ADOPT WITH TWO CHANGES (late-dissent adjudication) — The FLAGSHIP seat, LAST, on the late codex answers to #550, #551 and #549 (claude-fable-5-1 by agent_models.py, clean).  Verbatim head: &quot;ADOPT WITH TWO CHANGES -- ten dispositions plus L11: nine stand ... L3 is WRONG IN GRADE ... L10&#x27;s supporting sentence is FALSE as written&quot;.  No late finding names a measurement that would make it L2; #553 ships separately, before #529. — evidence: regress/artifacts/latecodex_20260926/fable5_latecodex.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 pass on pass 2 (its #550 VERDICT line) -- the Opus 5 MEASURING seat (Agent tool; claude-opus-5-5 throughout by agent_models.py, agent a8c6fd47...; every build in a scratch clone, GXEMUL-SEC untouched).  Same model family as the main loop: badge s.  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/opus5_f2b.md — record: 2026-09-18 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Pointer: this row was worked under `wiringcliff` as #536.  Its review is that row&#x27;s nine-seat pass 2 + §F2 (panel_20260918_190341, panel_20260918_193405).  The owner ruled the re-date to 2026-09-27, so the one-block cliff this row names is RE-CREATED a week out, deliberately and dated; the row stays open for exactly that.</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-26 — 1 of 11 dispositions wrong (L10, the record error the flagship and Astra correct — GPT-6 Astra (codex max, tools/cxlaunch.sh, pointer form) -- the independent codex twin of the flagship&#x27;s adjudication on the late codex answers&#x27; adjudication (latecodex_20260926/).  Its verdict, verbatim: 1 of 11 dispositions wrong (L10, the record error the flagship and Astra corrected); all 24 reset shapes red by reading, placement by placement; nine plus four measured; no floor breach. — evidence: regress/artifacts/latecodex_20260926/codex_jobs/codex_latecodexadv.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 2 (one panel with #551) (panel_20260925_163352, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/).  agy (FILE-READING, gemini-3.8-flash-high, 13151 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/agy.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — DEDICATED: SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the DEDICATED adversarial grok job on pass 2&#x27;s F2 (its #550 VERDICT line).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/f2b/grok_dedicated_f2b.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 2 (one panel with #551) (panel_20260925_163352, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/).  kimi (PACKET-FED, kimi-k3:cloud (the kimi CLI returned a subscription-access 403: kimi.txt), 8398 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/ollama_kimi.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 2 (one panel with #551) (panel_20260925_163352, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/).  glm (PACKET-FED, glm-5.3:cloud, 9087 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/ollama_glm.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 2 (one panel with #551) (panel_20260925_163352, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/).  deepseek (PACKET-FED, deepseek-v4-pro:cloud, 789 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/ollama_deepseek.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP WITH CHANGES — #550 the F2 adjudication pass on pass 2 (one panel with #551) (panel_20260925_163352, durable regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/).  minimax (PACKET-FED, minimax-m3:cloud, 8622 bytes).  Its verdict, verbatim: SHIP WITH CHANGES.  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #550 and regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/ (the F2 packets and the flagship rulings). — evidence: regress/artifacts/exemptredate_20260925/panels/panel_20260925_163352/ollama_minimax.txt</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — SHIP — #550 FINAL, the FLAGSHIP seat (regress is fable5-only): &quot;VERDICT #550: SHIP&quot; on v3 final, and the commit-plan hazard it found while verifying -- #549&#x27;s prepared committed versions predate #550 and would revert the ten re-dates; they are regenerated on top of #550 before #549 commits. — evidence: regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/fable_f2b/fable5_f2b_550_551.md</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">wiringshghost</span><span class="ttl">check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s manifest named three .sh paths while its domain() is .py-only by construction -- three permanently unsatisfiable GHOST rows holding the pre-commit gate red</span><span class="tip">check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s manifest named three .sh paths while its domain() is .py-only by construction -- three permanently unsatisfiable GHOST rows holding the pre-commit gate red — note: [2026-10-02] COMMITS FIELD LEFT EMPTY by #557, on purpose: no commit shipped the deletion of the three .sh manifest keys -- they existed only in a working tree and were never committed (686d179c&#x27;s parent 9c91999a has none of them); 686d179c RECORDS the resolution, adding the explanation at tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1157-1176, and is kept here as provenance only.  The attribution rule distinguishes shipped work from records about it (check_commit_attribution.py) and permits a documented-only closure with an empty field (Astra, aconf_557b item 2, correcting its census line and the first draft of this unit).  *** A CHECK THAT CANNOT PASS -- the mirror of the check-that-cannot-fail, and it had been holding the pre-commit gate RED. ***  check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s MANIFEST named three `.sh&#x27; paths (opus_close7_20260915/scripts2/{laneP,laneQ,mkfreeze}.sh, CLASS_TOOL, #529&#x27;s lane runners and instrument freezer).  Its `domain()&#x27; is `.py&#x27;-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION: it runs `git ls-files -- &quot;*.py&quot;&#x27; and filters `f.endswith(&quot;.py&quot;)&#x27; in two further places.  A `.sh&#x27; path can therefore NEVER enter the domain, so a `.sh&#x27; manifest entry reports GHOST *whatever its git state*.  MEASURED, which is how it was found rather than reasoned: all three were `git add&#x27;ed, `git ls-files&#x27; listed all three, and the checker still called them ghosts -- while the FIVE `.py&#x27; files in the SAME DIRECTORY cleared.  That asymmetry is the tell.  FIXED by DELETING the three entries and preserving their descriptions as a comment in place.  The alternative -- widening domain() to `.sh&#x27; -- was rejected on a stated measurement risk: every unclassified shell driver under regress/ would go newly red, a flood this check was never scoped for.  TWO CONTROLS, both run: (1) the checker goes 3 GHOSTs -&gt; 0 and PROBEWIRING_PASS; (2) the three files remain TRACKED, so the record is preserved and only an undischargeable obligation was removed.  A backup of the pre-edit checker is at /tmp/cpw.before.py for this session.</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — *** A CHECK THAT CANNOT PASS -- the mirror of the check-that-cannot-fail, and it had been holding the pre-commit gate RED. ***  check_probe_wiring.py&#x27;s MANIFEST named three `.sh&#x27; paths (opus_close7_20260915/scripts2/{laneP,laneQ,mkfreeze}.sh, CLASS_TOOL, #529&#x27;s lane runners and instrument freezer).  Its `domain()&#x27; is `.py&#x27;-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION: it runs `git ls-files -- &quot;*.py&quot;&#x27; and filters `f.endswith(&quot;.py&quot;)&#x27; in two further places.  A `.sh&#x27; path can therefore NEVER enter the domain, so a `.sh&#x27; manifest entry reports GHOST *whatever its git state*.  MEASURED, which is how it was found rather than reasoned: all three were `git add&#x27;ed, `git ls-files&#x27; listed all three, and the checker still called them ghosts -- while the FIVE `.py&#x27; files in the SAME DIRECTORY cleared.  That asymmetry is the tell.  FIXED by DELETING the three entries and preserving their descriptions as a comment in place.  The alternative -- widening domain() to `.sh&#x27; -- was rejected on a stated measurement risk: every unclassified shell driver under regress/ would go newly red, a flood this check was never scoped for.  TWO CONTROLS, both run: (1) the checker goes 3 GHOSTs -&gt; 0 and PROBEWIRING_PASS; (2) the three files remain TRACKED, so the record is preserved and only an undischargeable obligation was removed.  A backup of the pre-edit checker is at /tmp/cpw.before.py for this session. — evidence: tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py; PROBEWIRING_PASS after the edit</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">unreadseats23</span><span class="ttl">TWENTY-THREE real seat answers (~400 KB) across six panels of 2026-08-27 and 2026-09-07 are recorded nowhere and have never been read</span><span class="tip">TWENTY-THREE real seat answers (~400 KB) across six panels of 2026-08-27 and 2026-09-07 are recorded nowhere and have never been read — note: [2026-10-02] A MEMBER OF `closeassessrows` (#557, from the census: regress/artifacts/closeassess_20261002/grok/grok_closedcensus.txt; confirmed regress/artifacts/closeassess_20261002/aconf_census/codex_aconf_census.txt).  Work still alive: the 23 answers were read, and the same note leaves four checks undone (a gate that matches the probe&#x27;s printed strings; the PUT@8 contract overclaim; the `rgb not corrupt` inequality; no ABGR row) -- pending checks, not established defects (Astra: sgi_re_rgb_probe.py:343 already asserts the exact value).  The row is NOT re-opened here: that decision is the class row&#x27;s work.  Split out from the gate&#x27;s section-G count once the two THINKING BURNS were separated (see `seatsreadburnsplit&#x27;).  These 23 are REAL ANSWERS with non-empty response fields.  *** THIS PROJECT HAS NOW FOUND REAL DEFECTS IN AN UNREAD REVIEW FOUR TIMES -- most recently on 2026-09-18, when grok&#x27;s FIXDIFF prescription of `isr 28 rd val&#x27; turned out to have been written down before #531 shipped and cost an extra kill table to rediscover. ***  The single largest is panel_20260907_184039/ollama_glm at 243,346 chars, which is notable twice over: panel_ollama.py DETECTED a thinking burn on the first shot and re-fired with think=False to recover a 121 KB real answer -- so the tooling did its job and the answer was still never opened.  TRIAGED, NOT READ: this row exists because the 25-count was measured and split, not because the content was reviewed.  Reading them is the work.  Panels: 20260827_050852 (4), 20260827_134019 (5), 20260907_051055 (4), 20260907_104814 (3), 20260907_184039 (4), 20260907_221353 (3).  *** FOUR UNREAD SEAT ANSWERS FROM _scratchpad/panel_20260907_051055 READ 2026-09-18 -- the FIRST of the 23 to be opened, chosen because this panel is cited by a LIVE HIGH row. ***  They contain real content, which is the fifth time this project has found something in an unread review.  (1) *** THREE SEATS INDEPENDENTLY DERIVED THAT `+&#x27; -&gt; `|&#x27; IS AN UNCATCHABLE NULL MUTANT in the RGB pack: every term is a uint8_t shifted into DISJOINT bit ranges, so sum == OR always. ***  glm: &#x27;No test can or should catch it.&#x27;  kimi: &#x27;Uncatchable by construction.&#x27;  minimax: &#x27;NOT caught by behavioral tests.&#x27;  That is an EQUIVALENT mutant and therefore a RESULT, not a coverage gap -- the same disposition #531 reached for its latch-macro renumbering.  Three independent derivations is the one kind of agreement that IS evidence.  (2) glm AND kimi independently named a CLEAN-SWEEP mutant: the MIRROR EDIT IN THE PUT ARM (make PUT write [0,R,G,B]).  It round-trips perfectly against the corrected GET, so every round-trip row passes while the on-the-wire byte order is inverted.  A clause-(d) concern for whatever detector shipped.  (3) deepseek challenged a MEASURED VALUE and the resolution is PATH-DEPENDENT, which is worth more than either claim: it derived that an RGB PUT-&gt;GET round-trip on 0xaabbccdd yields **0xbbcc0000**, not the 0xbbccdd00 the records carry.  BOTH ARE CORRECT FOR DIFFERENT PATHS, verified here against dev_sgi_re.c: a COPY reads its source as four REAL bytes from guest memory (buf = {aa,bb,cc,dd}) so GET-reads-buf[1..3] gives 0xbbccdd00; a PUT-&gt;GET round-trip writes an explicit PAD at buf[3]=0 (the PUT arm sets it) so the same GET gives 0xbbcc0000.  **The defect, if any, is a record that quotes one path&#x27;s value while describing the other&#x27;s** -- NOT verified here which way #505&#x27;s brief put it, and deliberately NOT asserted.  Filed for checking.  (4) CORROBORATION OF TWO OPEN ROWS, from seats that had never been read: glm found &#x27;no arm initializes buf[4..7] -- a bufdepth-8 PUT transmits four uninitialised bytes&#x27; (= `sgirebufuninit&#x27;), and kimi found &#x27;all three 32-bit arms pack/unpack four bytes regardless of bufdepth, which can be 1, 2, 4 or 8&#x27; (= `sgirebufshiftub&#x27;).  kimi also independently re-found the YCRCB default writing four bytes of host random() (= `sgirandomcolour&#x27;, HIGH).  *** PROGRESS: 4 of 23 READ (panel_20260907_051055). NINETEEN REMAIN. ***  *** AN UNREAD REVIEW IS TIME-INDEXED, AND READING ONE LATE CAN MANUFACTURE PHANTOM WORK AS EASILY AS IT RECOVERS A DEFECT.  Measured 2026-09-18 on the second panel opened. ***  panel_20260907_184039: TWO seats independently (kimi and glm) flagged #507&#x27;s comment claim &#x27;here and three lines up&#x27; as FALSE, and glm named the actual lines it should cite.  glm went further -- &#x27;Q2: not shipped: #507 as written (comment)&#x27;.  A live L4 in a closed round, found by two seats, in an answer nobody had opened.  *** IT WAS ALREADY FIXED. ***  cpu_alpha_palcode.c now reads &#x27;four lines above&#x27; and carries its own correction note: &#x27;&quot;three lines up&quot; until 2026-09-07&#x27; -- the SAME DAY as that panel.  Verified here: `apcb_ptbr = new_ptbr&#x27; is at :296 and the #507 comment block begins at :300, so FOUR is right and THREE was wrong.  The seats were correct when they wrote it and the defect was discharged, almost certainly by a sibling answer that WAS read.  *** THE CONSEQUENCE FOR THE REMAINING 19, AND IT CHANGES HOW THEY MUST BE PROCESSED: these answers are up to THREE WEEKS OLD (2026-08-27 and 2026-09-07).  Every finding in them must be RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE CURRENT TREE before it is recorded as live.  The unread-review hazard is usually stated as &#x27;you miss real defects&#x27;; its mirror is &#x27;you re-raise fixed ones&#x27;, and a phantom row costs a round. ***  *Method for the rest, therefore: read for findings, then CHECK each against HEAD before filing -- exactly as the #507 claim was checked here rather than recorded on two seats&#x27; agreement.*  ALSO CAPTURED from that panel, still to check: kimi&#x27;s #506 `relative_addr&#x27; question, glm&#x27;s four per-round &#x27;single settling fact&#x27; items, and minimax&#x27;s observation on #508 that `return 2&#x27; reports every walked page writable.  *** PROGRESS: 8 of 23 READ.  FIFTEEN REMAIN. ***  *** THREE MORE UNREAD ANSWERS READ 2026-09-18 (panel_20260907_104814; its glm is one of the two THINKING BURNS and has nothing to read).  THE TIME-INDEXING LESSON LANDED A SECOND TIME AND MORE SHARPLY. ***  deepseek&#x27;s Q6 claimed the gate&#x27;s `^$v  .*ok$&#x27; row pattern CANNOT MATCH, because the probe pads `%-16s&#x27; plus a space so only a 15-char name leaves exactly two.  **MEASURED FALSE HERE**: the `.*&#x27; after the two literal spaces absorbs the extra padding, so every name of &lt;= 15 chars matches -- `rgb chan&#x27; (9 trailing spaces) matches True; only a name of 16+ fails.  kimi, in the SAME unread panel, had already corrected deepseek: an unsatisfiable pattern makes `count&#x27; return 0 against a wanted 1 and FAILS LOUDLY rather than greening.  *** AND gate_arm.sh ALREADY CARRIES THAT CORRECTION IN ITS OWN COMMENT, measured at name lengths 15/16/17, INCLUDING the note that an earlier draft had copied the wrong &#x27;silently stops testing while staying green&#x27; sentence from a sibling block and that the pass-2 panel caught it. ***  So the gate was already right and already knew.  **Had I recorded deepseek&#x27;s claim as a finding I would have filed a false defect against a gate that documents the opposite, with a measurement.**  Checked instead of recorded, per the method this row adopted after the #507 case.  WHAT SURVIVES, none of it yet checked against HEAD and all of it flagged as such: (1) kimi -- *** THE GATE BLOCK GREPS STRINGS THE PROBE ITSELF PRINTED (row verdicts, SGIRGB_WITNESS=PASS), so it validates the probe&#x27;s SELF-REPORT rather than independent behaviour -- &#x27;the probe grades its own homework&#x27;. ***  Real, but ARCHITECTURAL: it is how every probe-backed gate in this tree works, and the mitigation is that the probe&#x27;s rows are themselves measured against mutants.  Worth a row of its own rather than a #531 rider.  (2) deepseek -- CONTRACT OVERCLAIM: the row set has `rgb chan&#x27; (GET@4), `rgb depth64&#x27; (GET@8) and `rgb samemode&#x27; (PUT@4), and NO row for PUT@8, while the contract claims &#x27;both directions at widths 4 and 8&#x27;.  Its M9_put8 mutant corrupts the RGB PUT arm only when bufdepth == 8 and is predicted to sweep clean.  CHECKABLE.  (3) kimi -- `rgb not corrupt&#x27; is an INEQUALITY against one specific value (0xbbccdd00), so it greens on ANY other wrong value, including a different corruption.  (4) kimi -- value-conditioned and location-conditioned mutants; and NO ABGR row exists, so a reader assuming sibling coverage would be wrong.  *** PROGRESS: 11 of 23 READ.  TWELVE REMAIN. ***  *** FOUR MORE UNREAD ANSWERS READ 2026-09-18 (panel_20260827_050852).  THIS ONE IS A RATIFICATION, AND THAT IS RECORDED EXPLICITLY RATHER THAN LEFT BLANK -- the gate&#x27;s own rule: if a seat truly had nothing new to say, record THAT, because a blank cell and a seat failure must not look alike. ***  agy: VERDICT GO, &#x27;all premises, calculations, diff hunks and test oracles are verified against the repository&#x27;.  glm, minimax and deepseek concur.  NO live defect found, and none of the four raised a floor or coverage breach.  *** THE ONE SUBSTANTIVE CONVERGENCE, reached INDEPENDENTLY by agy and deepseek, and it is a warrant the round should keep: THE TWO DEFECTS WERE NOT SEPARABLE AND SHIPPING THEM TOGETHER WAS MANDATORY. ***  Bounding the initial push WITHOUT the re-arm refill would have made every transfer in (32768, 65536] worse than pre-fix: the initial push queues only 32768, the guest drains it, atapi_len goes 0, the re-arm then sets atapi_len = remaining while THE RING IS EMPTY -- so the guest is told bytes remain and none do.  That band WORKED pre-fix by accident (the whole transfer was pushed on the initial arm), so a half-fix would have INJECTED corruption into a working band.  glm&#x27;s one nit, a RECORDS point: the commit message states the re-arm fix is for the &gt;32768 remaining case and separately that bounding is for the &gt;262656 wrap, which reads as two independent fixes when the coupling is tighter than that.  Commit messages are immutable history, so this is noted rather than edited.  ALL FOUR independently confirmed the round&#x27;s SCOPE BLOCK is honest: a rung-1 direct-call harness is a DETECTOR and never a witness; only the FIRST re-arm is pinned; wdc_addtoinbuf() remains unbounded (filed); and *** wdcrearmzero STILL OWES A RUNG-3/4 WITNESS *** -- which is the one actionable item this panel leaves, and it is why the row is HELD rather than closed.  *** PROGRESS: 15 of 23 READ.  EIGHT REMAIN (panel_20260827_134019 x5 -&gt; wdcaltctrlbit [closed]; panel_20260907_221353 x3 -&gt; lcashiftub [closed/low]). ***  *** THREE MORE UNREAD ANSWERS READ 2026-09-18 (panel_20260907_221353), AND THEY CONVERGED ON ONE SETTLING FACT THAT NOBODY EVER LOOKED UP -- ONE GREP, ELEVEN DAYS UNREAD. ***  glm, kimi and minimax independently named THE SAME single missing fact as the only thing standing between the round and a clean pass: THE DECLARED TYPE OF `tag&#x27; in DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf).  kimi put it plainest: &#x27;What settles Q1 (the only open technical question): one line -- the declaration of `tag&#x27;.&#x27;  *** SETTLED 2026-09-18 BY READING IT: `int tag, type1, bus, dev, func, reg;&#x27; -- a plain int. ***  AND THE CONSEQUENCE, derived rather than asserted: in the fixed expression `tag &amp; (0x800U &lt;&lt; dev)&#x27; the UNSIGNED operand forces `tag&#x27; to be converted to unsigned int by the usual arithmetic conversions, so the AND is evaluated in unsigned and its TRUTH VALUE is identical to the pre-fix expression&#x27;s.  The fix removes the signed-overflow UB (`0x800 &lt;&lt; 20&#x27; on a plain int is 2^31, which does not fit) WITHOUT changing behaviour on any real target.  **THE ROUND&#x27;S UNIVERSAL NO-CHANGE CLAIM HOLDS**, and it is now settled by a reading rather than resting on an unverified premise -- which is what all three seats asked for.  OTHER POINTS THEY RAISED, none of them live defects: glm flagged P3 as &#x27;the round&#x27;s weakest settled premise -- asserted, uninlined, and precisely the shape seven seats ratified last time&#x27; (the premise-audit class, correctly identified); kimi noted a DUPLICATE CROSS-REFERENCE (the trailing /* #511 */ on the fixed line plus the citation inside the block -- keep one) and that the control&#x27;s 3/4 invariant score should be quoted in the `ubsanshiftlane&#x27; row as evidence; minimax noted `0x800U &lt;&lt; dev&#x27; is well-defined only if unsigned int is at least 32 bits, true on every host this project targets.  *** PROGRESS: 18 of 23 READ.  FIVE REMAIN (panel_20260827_134019, -&gt; wdcaltctrlbit [closed]). ***  *** THE LAST FIVE UNREAD ANSWERS READ 2026-09-18 (panel_20260827_134019).  23 OF 23 NOW READ -- the section-G backlog is CLEARED. ***  This was a pass-1 DESIGN panel on a now-CLOSED row, so it was read for the question `seatprescriptiondiff&#x27; exists to ask: DID THE PRESCRIPTIONS SURVIVE INTO THE SHIPPED WORK?  *** AND THE ANSWER IS YES -- A NEGATIVE RESULT THAT BOUNDS THE ROW I FILED THIS MORNING. ***  agy prescribed three items.  (1) the predicate fix -- SHIPPED, dev_wdc.c now triggers on WDCTL_RST (0x04) and not WDCTL_4BIT (0x08), with the rising-edge `prev_ctl&#x27; machinery and a recorded brace hazard beside it.  (2) the MACHINE_LANDISK alt-status mapping -- NOT in dev_wdc.c, and NOT a silent drop: it was SPLIT INTO ITS OWN ROW `landiskaux&#x27;, which is open, and OUTSTANDING_BUGS carries the coupling in full.  (3) acceptance rows -- folded, per the kimi/deepseek rulings in the same panel.  *** SO `seatprescriptiondiff&#x27; HAS A POPULATION OF ONE (the #531 case), NOT A PATTERN.  A class filed from a single instance is a hypothesis, and this is the first test of it -- it did not generalise.  Recorded as such rather than left looking systemic. ***  AND THE COUPLING WAS HANDLED IN THE SAFE ORDER, which is worth keeping because the unsafe one was live: mapping the landisk register WHILE the predicate still triggered on 0x08 would have latched COMMAND_RESET on SIX routine Device Control writes per probe (a seat measured twelve writes, six of them 0x08, currently all landing on unmapped memory).  The round fixed the PREDICATE first, so `wdcaltctrlbit&#x27; is CLOSED as overtaken and `landiskaux&#x27; is now OPEN AND UNBLOCKED.  *** THAT MAKES `landiskaux&#x27; A ONE-LINE FIX THAT IS NOW SAFE TO TAKE -- a strong critical-and-easily-resolvable candidate for the next round. ***  The other seats&#x27; content was design judgement, no live defects: glm listed SEVEN uninlined premises and ranked them by load-bearingness (the premise-audit discipline working as intended); minimax named an option-set hole (C4/B5, &#x27;the brief&#x27;s C-options jump&#x27;); deepseek ruled that a channel reset must clear in-flight transfer, FIFO, phase and interrupt state but NOT per-device-life diagnostics like `warned_*&#x27; -- and dev_wdc.c carries 43 `warned_&#x27; references, so that distinction is load-bearing there.  *** CLOSED 2026-09-18: ALL 23 READ.  Two were already-fixed or outright false when checked against HEAD, which is why the method was read-THEN-check; one settled an open question three seats had named (the `tag&#x27; type); one was a ratification recorded explicitly rather than left blank. ***</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — 23 real answers, ~400 KB, none read.  Two burns separated out and recorded as SEAT DOWN rather than as unread reviews. — evidence: scratchpad/precommit_b.out section G; the six panel dirs</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td cl