r, WIFEXITED &amp;&amp; status 1; a mid-session leg -- prologue verified live by a fresh reg, then quit, dead on the next interaction BEFORE cleanup, status 0; every surviving arm exit 0).  &#x27;nonexistent CSR: zeros, no error&#x27; is the VALUE warrant for a declined read; the diagnostic is policy.  fable5 D1/D4, 2026-09-19.  A codex design reading (cxfarm6 q1) was content-flagged; reword or route to grok. — commits: 4264ee20 — #545 fbdeclinefive CLOSED.  Five guest-reachable host kills in DEVICE_ACCESS(footbridge) -- writes to IRQ_STATUS, IRQ_RAW_STATUS, FIQ_STATUS, FIQ_RAW_STATUS and a read of IRQ_ENABLE_CLEAR -- are DECLINED and announced once per site (option-set member 3), witnessed at rung 3 (regress/footbridge_sites_probe.py on unmodified -E cats: each HOST-DIED pre-fix, 37/37 post-fix) and defended by regress/diff_footbridge.c at 864 rows (repair 3f, records-only over the tabled 3e) pinned by gate_offline.sh.  The detector&#x27;s chain ran repair 1, the class closure (repair 2) and repairs 3, 3c, 3d and 3e, and closed on 3e&#x27;s pass with the flagship seat&#x27;s final SHIP (q2_20260923/fable_final_20260923/FABLE_ANSWER.md).  Gates: the quiet-slot run (2026-09-23 22:19-23:34, nothing else on the machine): `run.sh 1 2 4 6` REGRESS_PASS -- gate 2&#x27;s footbridge rows 864 of 864 with every #545 family pin green (`offline-differential: PASS (357 checks)`), gate 6 PASS -- and gate 14 PASS (1054 checks) on this commit&#x27;s `gate_arm.sh` blob (HEAD plus #545&#x27;s two hunks; #529&#x27;s section excluded, so 1061 - 7), `regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/r3f_20260923/{gates_final,gate_arm}/`; the product file&#x27;s two-part clearance on all four trees (`r3f_20260923/clearance_final.out`).  What the detector does not cover is written in its contract and filed: fbirqstuck (with the producer pair, by owner ruling), fbenablewidth, fbclrdest, fbcallerctx, fblatchhistory, fbtimercomments, fbbufbounds, fbgateidentity; and from pass 1, armdesc3kill, armdacr2kill,