ression testing</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — SHIP — REGRESS stage, fired LAST: Fable 5.1, agent a6996d7e0077adfde, claude-fable-5-1 throughout (agent_models.py: no refusal, no fallback), FILE-READING, read-only.  F6e HAD NO PANEL PASS, by owner ruling (2026-09-23: one more pass, then file) -- this seat reviewed it, by name, with its controls (controls_c6e/).  VERDICT: SHIP.  Every classification right under the ruling: REAL and fixed -- codex&#x27;s swallowed close-time flush, the BOM parser read, the pty-leave deadlock, the messages; FILED -- the exotic inputs, the three F6-pass residues, and the non-atomic write as a post-pass finding in hygienecensusholes (a full disk is ordinary use, but F6e fails loudly and the gate is recoverable from git).  Conditions, all met before the commit: one F6e header sentence was FALSE (the change note is printable ASCII, not the ruling&#x27;s grammar) and one imprecise (which lists run under set -f) -- both corrected comment-only, deriver 77e190e9; the owed gate-6 run on the final files; census_tokens.py and derive_hygiene_pins.sh were UNTRACKED and are added by this commit; this record names the F6e review. — evidence: regress/artifacts/hygienecensus_20260923/fable_final_20260923/FABLE_ANSWER.md</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">upstreamdeleteprose</span><span class="ttl">dev_sgi_re.c&#x27;s #513 comment said `delete the kill`, so upstream&#x27;s test/check_delete_calls.