.\tools\pipeline\ledger.json:62598:   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09: the codex seat (GPT-6 Astra) was refused twice on armmmuvehicle's pass-1 brief (the second time a neutral, read-scoped rewrite); tools/cxlaunch.sh printed 'ROUTE THIS BRIEF TO GROK' (rc 7) -- `grep -n daybreak tools/*.sh` finds only panel.sh's comment.  The owner's 2026-10-01 fallback (gpt-daybreak-blue-latest on an Astra AUP refusal) lives only in _scratchpad/codexpack_20260928/cxlaunch_pack.run-*.sh, which answered the same brief on Daybreak.  Fix: give cxlaunch.sh that fallback; correct panel.sh's comment when it is next reviewed (it carries unreviewed deltas).  The memory file was corrected the same day.",
.\tools\pipeline\ledger.json:62665:   "id": "cxlaunchquotation",
.\tools\pipeline\ledger.json:62670:   "title": "tools/cxlaunch.sh's wall check greps the seat's ANSWER for 'quota', which matches 'quotation': a complete answer is reported SEAT WALLED and the launcher exits 8",
.\tools\pipeline\ledger.json:62671:   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09: measured on GPT-6 Astra's check of the asiceventaddr convergence -- a complete 10,466-byte answer with its verdict line, no `ERROR:` line on stderr, and the launcher printed 'SEAT WALLED' (LAUNCH_RC=8) because the answer's own sentence '... its quotation must retain ...' matched `grep -ic 'quota'` (the answer: regress/artifacts/fablequeue8n_20261009/astra_confirm/codex_astra_asicconverge.txt; the launcher's own output: cxlaunch_asicconverge_stdout.txt beside it).  tools/cxlaunch.sh:44 builds `wall` from the `ERROR:` lines PLUS the whole stdout, so any answer that uses the words quota / quotation / rate limit / usage limit reads as a wall -- the carrier's quoting-re-arms-the-reader class, one level down (the script's own comment at :33-41 diagnoses the stderr half and kept the stdout half).  Fix: word-anchor the pattern and test stdout only when no verdict line is present; owes controls both ways (a real 403/quota notice still reds; an answer containing 'quotation' does not).  LOW: a human reads the answer; an unattended runner would discard it."
.\tools\panel.sh:123:CODEX_EFFORT="ultra"        # OWNER DIRECTIVE 2026-09-26: "Astra (ultra)".  MEASURED before this edit: the server's enum is 'none'..'xhigh','max' and a bogus value is rejected 400 invalid_enum_value; `ultra` is ACCEPTED (rc 0, header "reasoning effort: ultra", liveness token + verbatim CHECKPOINT.md quote).  The CLI's model cache calls it "Maximum reasoning with automatic task delegation" -- a CLI tier above max.  (Was "max" by OWNER DIRECTIVE 2026-09-04.)  On a content-filter refusal re-fire the brief through tools/cxlaunch.sh, whose Daybreak fallback (gpt-daybreak-blue-latest, owner 2026-09-26) re-runs it once.
